DATA.push({"c":"toeic","l":2,"w":[["reimburse","/ˌriːɪmˈbɝːs/","v.","報銷、償還","The company will reimburse your travel expenses.","公司會報銷你的差旅費。"],["revenue","/ˈrevənuː/","n.","營收","Revenue rose 12% this quarter.","本季營收成長 12%。"],["expense","/ɪkˈspens/","n.","費用、開支","Keep all receipts for business expenses.","所有出差開支都要保留收據。"],["estimate","/ˈestɪmət/","n.","估價、估計","Can you give me a rough estimate?","你可以給我一個大概的估價嗎？"],["inventory","/ˈɪnvəntɔːri/","n.","庫存","We check our inventory every Friday.","我們每週五盤點庫存。"],["merchandise","/ˈmɝːtʃəndaɪs/","n.","商品","All merchandise is 20% off this week.","本週所有商品打八折。"],["warranty","/ˈwɔːrənti/","n.","保固","The printer comes with a two-year warranty.","這台印表機有兩年保固。"],["defective","/dɪˈfektɪv/","adj.","有瑕疵的","Defective items can be returned within 30 days.","瑕疵品可在 30 天內退回。"],["complimentary","/ˌkɑːmplɪˈmentəri/","adj.","免費贈送的","Breakfast is complimentary for all guests.","所有住客都享有免費早餐。"],["renovation","/ˌrenəˈveɪʃən/","n.","整修","The lobby is closed for renovation.","大廳因整修暫停開放。"],["relocate","/ˌriːˈloʊkeɪt/","v.","搬遷、調職","Our office will relocate to Neihu next year.","我們辦公室明年搬到內湖。"],["promote","/prəˈmoʊt/","v.","升遷；促銷","She was promoted to sales manager.","她升為業務經理。"],["candidate","/ˈkændɪdət/","n.","候選人、人選","He is the best candidate for the position.","他是這個職位的最佳人選。"],["qualified","/ˈkwɑːlɪfaɪd/","adj.","有資格的、合格的","We're looking for qualified engineers.","我們在找合格的工程師。"],["submit","/səbˈmɪt/","v.","提交","Please submit the report by Friday.","請在週五前交報告。"],["approve","/əˈpruːv/","v.","核准","The manager approved the budget.","經理核准了預算。"],["postpone","/poʊstˈpoʊn/","v.","延期","The event has been postponed until May.","活動延到五月。"],["agenda","/əˈdʒendə/","n.","議程","What's on the agenda for today's meeting?","今天會議的議程是什麼？"],["attendee","/əˌtenˈdiː/","n.","出席者","All attendees will receive a certificate.","所有出席者都會拿到證書。"],["register","/ˈredʒɪstɚ/","v.","報名、註冊","You can register online.","你可以線上報名。"],["regarding","/rɪˈɡɑːrdɪŋ/","prep.","關於","I'm writing regarding your recent order.","我寫信是關於您最近的訂單。"],["in charge of","/ɪn ˈtʃɑːrdʒ əv/","phr.","負責","Who is in charge of this project?","誰負責這個專案？"],["on behalf of","/ɑːn bɪˈhæf əv/","phr.","代表","I'm calling on behalf of Mr. Chen.","我代表陳先生打來。"],["due to","/ˈduː tuː/","phr.","由於","The flight was canceled due to bad weather.","班機因天候不佳取消。"],["vendor","/ˈvendɚ/","n.","供應商、廠商","We are comparing prices from three vendors.","我們在比較三家廠商的價格。"],["quarterly","/ˈkwɔːrtɚli/","adj.","每季的","The quarterly meeting is next Tuesday.","季會在下週二。"],["subscription","/səbˈskrɪpʃən/","n.","訂閱","Your subscription will expire next month.","您的訂閱下個月到期。"],["policy","/ˈpɑːləsi/","n.","政策、規定","Please read our return policy.","請閱讀我們的退貨規定。"],["confidential","/ˌkɑːnfɪˈdenʃl/","adj.","機密的","This information is strictly confidential.","這份資料嚴格保密。"],["proceed","/proʊˈsiːd/","v.","進行、繼續","Please proceed to Gate 12.","請前往 12 號登機門。"],["recruiter","/rɪˈkruːtər/","n.","招募人員","A recruiter called me about a sales position.","一位招募人員打給我談業務職缺。"],["recruitment","/rɪˈkruːtmənt/","n.","招募","Recruitment for the new branch starts in June.","新分公司的招募將於六月開始。"],["job applicant","/ˈdʒɑːb ˌæplɪkənt/","phr.","求職者","Each job applicant must take a short test.","每位求職者都需參加簡短測驗。"],["job posting","/ˈdʒɑːb ˌpoʊstɪŋ/","phr.","職缺公告","The job posting closes on March 15.","職缺公告於三月十五日截止。"],["job fair","/ˈdʒɑːb ˌfer/","phr.","就業博覽會","We met many strong candidates at the job fair.","我們在就業博覽會上遇到許多優秀人選。"],["opening","/ˈoʊpənɪŋ/","n.","職缺；開幕","We have an opening in the accounting team.","我們會計組有一個職缺。"],["fill a position","/ˌfɪl ə pəˈzɪʃən/","phr.","補實職缺","We hope to fill the position by next month.","我們希望下個月前補實這個職缺。"],["shortlist","/ˈʃɔːrtlɪst/","n./v.","候選名單；列入決選","Five applicants were shortlisted for interviews.","五位應徵者進入面試名單。"],["screen","/skriːn/","v.","篩選","HR screens all resumes before interviews.","人資部在面試前會篩選所有履歷。"],["interviewer","/ˈɪntərvjuːər/","n.","面試官","The interviewer asked about my past projects.","面試官詢問我過去的專案。"],["interviewee","/ˌɪntərvjuˈiː/","n.","受面試者","Each interviewee will meet three managers.","每位受面試者會與三位經理面談。"],["background check","/ˈbækgraʊnd ˌtʃek/","phr.","背景調查","The offer depends on a background check.","錄取與否取決於背景調查。"],["reference check","/ˈrefərəns ˌtʃek/","phr.","諮詢推薦人","We completed the reference check yesterday.","我們昨天完成了推薦人查核。"],["referee","/ˌrefəˈriː/","n.","推薦人","Please list two referees on your application.","請在申請表上列出兩位推薦人。"],["work history","/ˈwɝːk ˌhɪstəri/","phr.","工作經歷","Describe your work history in detail.","請詳細說明你的工作經歷。"],["certificate","/sərˈtɪfɪkət/","n.","證書","Attach a copy of your language certificate.","請附上語言證書影本。"],["certified","/ˈsɝːtɪfaɪd/","adj.","經認證的","We only hire certified accountants.","我們只雇用有證照的會計師。"],["license","/ˈlaɪsəns/","n.","執照","A driver's license is required for this job.","這份工作需要駕照。"],["preferred","/prɪˈfɝːd/","adj.","優先考慮的","Experience in sales is preferred.","有業務經驗者優先。"],["fluent","/ˈfluːənt/","adj.","流利的","She is fluent in English and Japanese.","她的英文和日文都很流利。"],["entry-level","/ˈentri ˌlevəl/","adj.","初階的、新手的","This is an entry-level position for graduates.","這是給畢業生的初階職位。"],["senior","/ˈsiːnjər/","adj.","資深的；高階的","She was promoted to senior engineer.","她升任資深工程師。"],["junior","/ˈdʒuːnjər/","adj.","資淺的；初級的","The junior staff attend training every Friday.","初級員工每週五參加培訓。"],["new hire","/ˌnuː ˈhaɪər/","phr.","新進員工","All new hires attend a welcome lunch.","所有新進員工都參加歡迎午宴。"],["onboarding","/ˈɑːnbɔːrdɪŋ/","n.","新進員工培訓、到職流程","Onboarding takes about two weeks.","到職流程大約需要兩週。"],["orientation session","/ˌɔːriənˈteɪʃən ˌseʃən/","phr.","新人說明會","The orientation session starts at nine sharp.","新人說明會九點整開始。"],["mentor","/ˈmentɔːr/","n./v.","導師；指導","Each new hire is assigned a mentor.","每位新人都會分配一位導師。"],["mentoring","/ˈmentɔːrɪŋ/","n.","輔導、指導制度","Our mentoring program helps new staff adjust.","我們的輔導計畫幫助新員工適應。"],["coach","/koʊtʃ/","v./n.","指導；教練","Managers coach their teams on sales skills.","經理指導團隊的銷售技巧。"],["on-the-job training","/ˌɑːn ðə ˈdʒɑːb ˌtreɪnɪŋ/","phr.","在職訓練","Most skills are learned through on-the-job training.","大部分技能透過在職訓練學習。"],["training session","/ˈtreɪnɪŋ ˌseʃən/","phr.","培訓課程","The training session was moved to Room B.","培訓課程改到 B 會議室。"],["employee handbook","/ɪmˈplɔɪiː ˌhændbʊk/","phr.","員工手冊","The leave policy is explained in the employee handbook.","休假政策在員工手冊中有說明。"],["instructor","/ɪnˈstrʌktər/","n.","講師","The instructor has twenty years of experience.","這位講師有二十年經驗。"],["enroll","/ɪnˈroʊl/","v.","報名、註冊","Fifteen employees enrolled in the course.","有十五位員工報名了這門課。"],["enrollment","/ɪnˈroʊlmənt/","n.","報名、註冊人數","Enrollment for the workshop closes Friday.","研習會報名週五截止。"],["attendance","/əˈtendəns/","n.","出席；出席人數","Attendance at the safety meeting is required.","安全會議必須出席。"],["professional development","/prəˈfeʃənəl dɪˈveləpmənt/","phr.","專業發展","We offer a budget for professional development.","我們提供專業發展預算。"],["skill set","/ˈskɪl ˌset/","n.","技能組合","Her skill set fits the role perfectly.","她的技能完全符合這個職務。"],["hands-on","/ˌhændz ˈɑːn/","adj.","實作的、親自動手的","The workshop includes hands-on practice.","研習會包含實作練習。"],["evaluation","/ɪˌvæljuˈeɪʃən/","n.","評估、考核","Please fill out the course evaluation form.","請填寫課程評估表。"],["assessment","/əˈsesmənt/","n.","評估","The assessment measures basic computer skills.","這項評估檢測基本電腦技能。"],["step down","/ˌstep ˈdaʊn/","phr.","辭職、下台","The CEO will step down at the end of the year.","執行長將於年底卸任。"],["resignation","/ˌrezɪgˈneɪʃən/","n.","辭職；辭呈","She handed in her resignation on Monday.","她週一遞出辭呈。"],["resignation letter","/ˌrezɪgˈneɪʃən ˌletər/","phr.","辭職信","Please submit a resignation letter to HR.","請向人資部提交辭職信。"],["notice period","/ˈnoʊtɪs ˌpɪriəd/","phr.","離職預告期","The notice period is one month.","離職預告期為一個月。"],["give notice","/ˌgɪv ˈnoʊtɪs/","phr.","提出離職預告","He gave notice two weeks before leaving.","他在離職前兩週提出預告。"],["exit interview","/ˈegzɪt ˌɪntərvjuː/","phr.","離職面談","All departing staff have an exit interview.","所有離職員工都要進行離職面談。"],["fire","/faɪər/","v.","解雇","He was fired for repeated lateness.","他因多次遲到被解雇。"],["dismissal","/dɪsˈmɪsəl/","n.","解雇","The dismissal followed a long investigation.","經過長期調查後予以解雇。"],["benefits package","/ˈbenɪfɪts ˌpækɪdʒ/","phr.","福利方案","The job comes with a generous benefits package.","這份工作附帶優渥的福利方案。"],["health insurance","/ˈhelθ ɪnˌʃʊrəns/","phr.","健康保險","Full-time staff receive health insurance.","全職員工享有健康保險。"],["pension plan","/ˈpenʃən ˌplæn/","phr.","退休金計畫","The company contributes to your pension plan.","公司會提撥到你的退休金計畫。"],["annual leave","/ˈænjuəl ˌliːv/","phr.","年假","I have five days of annual leave left.","我還剩五天年假。"],["personal day","/ˈpɝːsənəl ˌdeɪ/","phr.","事假","I'm taking a personal day on Friday.","我週五請事假。"],["paternity leave","/pəˈtɝːnəti ˌliːv/","phr.","陪產假","He will take paternity leave next month.","他下個月將請陪產假。"],["unpaid leave","/ʌnˈpeɪd ˌliːv/","phr.","無薪假","She took unpaid leave to care for her father.","她請無薪假照顧父親。"],["perk","/pɝːk/","n.","額外津貼、福利","Free parking is one of the perks of the job.","免費停車是這份工作的福利之一。"],["fringe benefits","/ˈfrɪndʒ ˌbenɪfɪts/","phr.","附加福利","Fringe benefits include a gym membership.","附加福利包含健身房會員。"],["allowance","/əˈlaʊəns/","n.","津貼","Staff receive a monthly travel allowance.","員工每月領有交通津貼。"],["year-end bonus","/ˌjɪr end ˈboʊnəs/","phr.","年終獎金","Everyone got a year-end bonus this year.","今年每個人都拿到年終獎金。"],["starting salary","/ˈstɑːrtɪŋ ˌsæləri/","phr.","起薪","The starting salary is higher than last year.","起薪比去年高。"],["base salary","/ˈbeɪs ˌsæləri/","phr.","底薪","Sales staff earn a base salary plus commission.","業務人員領底薪加佣金。"],["hourly wage","/ˈaʊərli ˌweɪdʒ/","phr.","時薪","The hourly wage for part-timers went up.","兼職人員的時薪調漲了。"],["minimum wage","/ˈmɪnɪməm ˌweɪdʒ/","phr.","最低工資","The minimum wage rises next January.","最低工資明年一月調漲。"],["overtime pay","/ˈoʊvərtaɪm ˌpeɪ/","phr.","加班費","Overtime pay is one and a half times normal.","加班費是平常的一點五倍。"],["work overtime","/ˌwɝːk ˈoʊvərtaɪm/","phr.","加班","We had to work overtime to meet the deadline.","為了趕截止日，我們必須加班。"],["direct deposit","/dəˌrekt dɪˈpɑːzɪt/","phr.","薪資直接入帳","Salaries are paid by direct deposit.","薪資以直接匯入帳戶方式發放。"],["take-home pay","/ˈteɪk hoʊm ˌpeɪ/","phr.","實領薪資","My take-home pay is lower after taxes.","扣稅後我的實領薪資較少。"],["timesheet","/ˈtaɪmʃiːt/","n.","工時表","Submit your timesheet every Friday afternoon.","請每週五下午繳交工時表。"],["clock in","/ˌklɑːk ˈɪn/","phr.","上班打卡","Remember to clock in when you arrive.","到公司時記得打卡。"],["clock out","/ˌklɑːk ˈaʊt/","phr.","下班打卡","Don't forget to clock out before you leave.","離開前別忘了打卡下班。"],["flexible hours","/ˈfleksəbəl ˈaʊərz/","phr.","彈性工時","Parents appreciate our flexible hours.","家長們很感謝我們的彈性工時。"],["work remotely","/ˌwɝːk rɪˈmoʊtli/","phr.","遠端工作","Staff may work remotely twice a week.","員工每週可遠端工作兩天。"],["telecommuting","/ˈteləkəˌmjuːtɪŋ/","n.","遠距工作","Telecommuting has reduced our office costs.","遠距工作降低了我們的辦公室成本。"],["absent","/ˈæbsənt/","adj.","缺席的","Three employees were absent with the flu.","三位員工因流感缺席。"],["absence","/ˈæbsəns/","n.","缺席；不在","In my absence, please contact Ms. Tsai.","我不在時，請聯絡蔡小姐。"],["absenteeism","/ˌæbsənˈtiːɪzəm/","n.","曠職、缺勤率","Absenteeism dropped after the wellness program.","推出健康計畫後缺勤率下降了。"],["tardy","/ˈtɑːrdi/","adj.","遲到的","Employees who are tardy must inform HR.","遲到的員工必須通知人資。"],["cover for","/ˈkʌvər fɔːr/","phr.","代班、頂替","Can you cover for me this afternoon?","你今天下午可以幫我代班嗎？"],["stand in for","/ˌstænd ˈɪn fɔːr/","phr.","代替","Mr. Ho will stand in for the director.","何先生將代替處長出席。"],["swap shifts","/ˌswɑːp ˈʃɪfts/","phr.","調班","Can we swap shifts next Saturday?","我們下週六可以調班嗎？"],["roster","/ˈrɑːstər/","n.","值班表；名冊","The weekly roster is on the wall.","每週值班表貼在牆上。"],["job rotation","/ˈdʒɑːb roʊˌteɪʃən/","phr.","輪調","Job rotation helps staff learn new skills.","輪調能幫助員工學習新技能。"],["workplace","/ˈwɝːkpleɪs/","n.","工作場所","We want a safe and friendly workplace.","我們希望有安全友善的工作環境。"],["dependable","/dɪˈpendəbəl/","adj.","可靠的","We need dependable staff for the night shift.","夜班需要可靠的員工。"],["motivated","/ˈmoʊtɪveɪtɪd/","adj.","有幹勁的","We seek motivated people who love challenges.","我們在找喜歡挑戰、有幹勁的人。"],["detail-oriented","/ˈdiːteɪl ˌɔːrientɪd/","adj.","注重細節的","The ideal candidate is detail-oriented.","理想人選需注重細節。"],["organized","/ˈɔːrgənaɪzd/","adj.","有條理的","An assistant must be well organized.","助理必須很有條理。"],["team player","/ˈtiːm ˌpleɪər/","phr.","有團隊精神的人","We are looking for a true team player.","我們在找真正有團隊精神的人。"],["self-starter","/ˌself ˈstɑːrtər/","n.","主動積極的人","The job suits a self-starter who works independently.","這份工作適合能獨立作業、主動積極的人。"],["multitask","/ˌmʌltiˈtæsk/","v.","同時處理多項工作","Receptionists must multitask all day.","接待人員整天都要同時處理多項工作。"],["communication skills","/kəˌmjuːnɪˈkeɪʃən ˌskɪlz/","phr.","溝通能力","Strong communication skills are essential.","良好的溝通能力是必要的。"],["interpersonal skills","/ˌɪntərˈpɝːsənəl ˌskɪlz/","phr.","人際能力","Sales staff need excellent interpersonal skills.","業務人員需要優秀的人際能力。"],["leadership","/ˈliːdərʃɪp/","n.","領導力","She showed strong leadership on the project.","她在專案中展現出強大的領導力。"],["supervision","/ˌsuːpərˈvɪʒən/","n.","監督、管理","Interns work under close supervision.","實習生在嚴密監督下工作。"],["subordinate","/səˈbɔːrdənət/","n.","部屬","A good manager listens to subordinates.","好主管會傾聽部屬的意見。"],["report to","/rɪˈpɔːrt tuː/","phr.","向……匯報、隸屬於","You will report to the sales manager.","你將直屬業務經理。"],["direct report","/dəˌrekt rɪˈpɔːrt/","phr.","直屬部屬","She has six direct reports.","她有六位直屬部屬。"],["return a call","/rɪˌtɝːn ə ˈkɔːl/","phr.","回電","Please return my call as soon as you can.","請盡快回我電話。"],["call in sick","/ˌkɔːl ɪn ˈsɪk/","phr.","打電話請病假","Two drivers called in sick this morning.","今天早上有兩位司機打電話請病假。"],["hold the line","/ˌhoʊld ðə ˈlaɪn/","phr.","請稍候（不要掛斷）","Please hold the line while I check.","我確認一下，請稍候。"],["get through","/ˌget ˈθruː/","phr.","（電話）打通","I couldn't get through to the main office.","我打不通總公司的電話。"],["reach","/riːtʃ/","v.","聯絡上","You can reach me at extension 205.","你可以打分機 205 找我。"],["get in touch with","/ˌget ɪn ˈtʌtʃ wɪð/","phr.","與……聯絡","I'll get in touch with the candidate today.","我今天會與候選人聯絡。"],["cc","/ˌsiː ˈsiː/","v.","副本抄送","Please cc me on your reply to the client.","回覆客戶時請副本給我。"],["out-of-office reply","/ˌaʊt əv ˈɔːfɪs rɪˌplaɪ/","phr.","自動休假回覆","Set an out-of-office reply before your trip.","出差前請設定自動休假回覆。"],["interoffice","/ˌɪntərˈɔːfɪs/","adj.","公司內部的","Send it by interoffice mail.","請以內部郵件寄送。"],["circulate","/ˈsɝːkjəleɪt/","v.","傳閱","Please circulate this memo to your team.","請將這份備忘錄傳閱給你的團隊。"],["bulletin","/ˈbʊlətɪn/","n.","公告；簡報","Read the weekly bulletin for company news.","閱讀每週公告了解公司消息。"],["intranet","/ˈɪntrənet/","n.","內部網路","Forms are available on the company intranet.","表格可在公司內網取得。"],["portal","/ˈpɔːrtəl/","n.","入口網站","Log in to the employee portal to view your pay.","登入員工入口網站查看薪資。"],["regards","/rɪˈgɑːrdz/","n.","問候（信末）","Best regards, and thank you for your time.","敬祝安好，感謝您撥冗。"],["sincerely","/sɪnˈsɪrli/","adv.","謹啟；真誠地","We sincerely thank you for applying.","我們誠摯感謝您的應徵。"],["to whom it may concern","/tə ˌhuːm ɪt meɪ kənˈsɝːn/","phr.","敬啟者","To whom it may concern, I am writing to apply.","敬啟者：我寫信是為了應徵。"],["please find attached","/pliːz ˌfaɪnd əˈtætʃt/","phr.","隨信附上","Please find attached my updated resume.","隨信附上我更新後的履歷。"],["rearrange","/ˌriːəˈreɪndʒ/","v.","重新安排","Can we rearrange the meeting for Thursday?","我們可以把會議改到週四嗎？"],["move up","/ˌmuːv ˈʌp/","phr.","提前","The interview was moved up to ten.","面試提前到十點。"],["push back","/ˌpʊʃ ˈbæk/","phr.","延後","Let's push back the training by one week.","我們把培訓延後一週吧。"],["double-book","/ˌdʌbəl ˈbʊk/","v.","重複預約","Sorry, I double-booked myself on Monday.","抱歉，我週一重複約了時間。"],["fully booked","/ˌfʊli ˈbʊkt/","phr.","已排滿","The manager is fully booked this week.","經理這週行程已排滿。"],["hiring freeze","/ˈhaɪərɪŋ ˌfriːz/","phr.","凍結招聘","There is a hiring freeze until next quarter.","下一季之前凍結招聘。"],["staff turnover","/ˈstæf ˌtɝːnoʊvər/","phr.","員工流動","We want to reduce staff turnover.","我們希望降低員工流動率。"],["employee of the month","/ɪmˈplɔɪiː əv ðə ˈmʌnθ/","phr.","本月最佳員工","Mia was named employee of the month.","Mia 獲選為本月最佳員工。"],["recognition","/ˌrekəgˈnɪʃən/","n.","表揚、認可","The award is in recognition of her hard work.","這個獎是為了表揚她的努力。"],["recruiting","/rɪˈkruːtɪŋ/","n.","招募","Recruiting top talent is our main challenge.","招募頂尖人才是我們的主要挑戰。"],["nominee","/ˌnɑːmɪˈniː/","n.","被提名人","The nominees for the award were announced.","獎項的被提名人已公布。"],["nominate","/ˈnɑːmɪneɪt/","v.","提名","She was nominated for employee of the year.","她被提名為年度最佳員工。"],["applicable","/əˈplɪkəbəl/","adj.","適用的","Fill in all applicable sections of the form.","請填寫表格所有適用的欄位。"],["diploma","/dɪˈploʊmə/","n.","畢業證書；文憑","Bring a copy of your diploma to the interview.","面試時請攜帶畢業證書影本。"],["major in","/ˈmeɪdʒər ɪn/","phr.","主修","She majored in accounting at college.","她大學主修會計。"],["transcript","/ˈtrænskrɪpt/","n.","成績單；文字紀錄","Applicants must submit an official transcript.","應徵者必須提交正式成績單。"],["portfolio","/pɔːrtˈfoʊlioʊ/","n.","作品集","Designers should bring a portfolio to the interview.","設計師面試時應攜帶作品集。"],["qualify for","/ˈkwɑːləfaɪ fɔːr/","phr.","有資格（得到）","You qualify for a bonus after one year.","任職滿一年就有資格領獎金。"],["suitable","/ˈsuːtəbəl/","adj.","適合的","We haven't found a suitable candidate yet.","我們還沒找到合適的人選。"],["selection","/sɪˈlekʃən/","n.","選拔；挑選","The selection process takes four weeks.","甄選流程需要四週。"],["finalist","/ˈfaɪnəlɪst/","n.","決選者","Three finalists were invited for a second interview.","三位決選者受邀參加二次面試。"],["supervisory","/ˌsuːpərˈvaɪzəri/","adj.","管理的、監督的","She has five years of supervisory experience.","她有五年的管理經驗。"],["managerial","/ˌmænəˈdʒɪriəl/","adj.","管理的、經理的","He is ready for a managerial position.","他已準備好擔任管理職。"],["demote","/dɪˈmoʊt/","v.","降職","He was demoted after the poor review.","考核不佳後他被降職。"],["advancement","/ədˈvænsmənt/","n.","晉升、發展","The job offers chances for advancement.","這份工作有晉升機會。"],["achievement","/əˈtʃiːvmənt/","n.","成就","Her achievements were praised at the meeting.","她的成就在會議上受到讚揚。"],["praise","/preɪz/","v./n.","稱讚","The manager praised the team for its hard work.","經理稱讚團隊的努力。"],["dedication","/ˌdedɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","奉獻、投入","We thank her for her dedication to the company.","我們感謝她對公司的投入。"],["effort","/ˈefərt/","n.","努力","Thank you for your effort on this project.","感謝你為這個專案的努力。"],["diligently","/ˈdɪlɪdʒəntli/","adv.","勤奮地","She worked diligently to train the new staff.","她勤奮地培訓新員工。"],["competence","/ˈkɑːmpɪtəns/","n.","能力、勝任","The test measures basic competence in English.","這項測驗衡量基本英文能力。"],["capability","/ˌkeɪpəˈbɪləti/","n.","能力","We need to improve our staff's capabilities.","我們需要提升員工的能力。"],["expert","/ˈekspɝːt/","n.","專家","An HR expert will lead the workshop.","研習會將由一位人資專家主持。"],["specialist","/ˈspeʃəlɪst/","n.","專員；專家","She works as a payroll specialist.","她擔任薪資專員。"],["coordinator","/koʊˈɔːrdɪneɪtər/","n.","協調人、專員","The training coordinator booked the room.","培訓專員預訂了會議室。"],["officer","/ˈɔːfɪsər/","n.","主管；官員","Talk to the personnel officer about your leave.","請假的事請洽人事主管。"],["associate","/əˈsoʊʃiət/","n.","同事；助理職員","Our sales associates are paid weekly.","我們的銷售助理每週領薪。"],["crew","/kruː/","n.","一組工作人員","The cleaning crew comes in at night.","清潔人員晚上進來。"],["labor","/ˈleɪbər/","n.","勞工；勞動","Labor costs have gone up this year.","今年人力成本上升了。"],["manpower","/ˈmænpaʊər/","n.","人力","We lack the manpower to finish on time.","我們缺乏準時完成的人力。"],["overworked","/ˌoʊvərˈwɝːkt/","adj.","過勞的","Many nurses feel overworked and underpaid.","許多護理師覺得工作過量又薪水過低。"],["underpaid","/ˌʌndərˈpeɪd/","adj.","薪資過低的","The survey found many workers feel underpaid.","調查發現許多員工覺得薪資過低。"],["well-paid","/ˌwel ˈpeɪd/","adj.","高薪的","It's a well-paid job with good benefits.","這是一份高薪又福利好的工作。"],["earnings","/ˈɝːnɪŋz/","n.","收入","Her earnings increased after the promotion.","升職後她的收入增加了。"],["unpaid","/ʌnˈpeɪd/","adj.","無薪的；未付的","The internship is unpaid but very useful.","這份實習沒有薪水但很有幫助。"],["deduct","/dɪˈdʌkt/","v.","扣除","Taxes are deducted from your monthly pay.","稅金會從月薪中扣除。"],["calculate","/ˈkælkjəleɪt/","v.","計算","Payroll calculates overtime automatically.","薪資系統會自動計算加班費。"],["coverage","/ˈkʌvərɪdʒ/","n.","保險範圍；涵蓋","The plan offers full coverage for dental care.","此方案全額給付牙科治療。"],["daycare","/ˈdeɪker/","n.","托兒服務","The company offers free daycare for staff.","公司為員工提供免費托兒服務。"],["code of conduct","/ˌkoʊd əv ˈkɑːndʌkt/","phr.","行為準則","All employees must follow the code of conduct.","所有員工都必須遵守行為準則。"],["violate","/ˈvaɪəleɪt/","v.","違反","Sharing passwords violates company policy.","分享密碼違反公司政策。"],["violation","/ˌvaɪəˈleɪʃən/","n.","違反","This is a violation of safety rules.","這違反了安全規定。"],["warning","/ˈwɔːrnɪŋ/","n.","警告","He received a written warning for lateness.","他因遲到收到書面警告。"],["lateness","/ˈleɪtnəs/","n.","遲到","Lateness will be noted in your review.","遲到會記錄在你的考核中。"],["excuse","/ɪkˈskjuːs/","n.","藉口；理由","Traffic is not an excuse for missing the meeting.","塞車不是缺席會議的理由。"],["postponement","/poʊstˈpoʊnmənt/","n.","延期","We apologize for the postponement of the seminar.","研討會延期，我們深感抱歉。"],["booked","/bʊkt/","adj.","已預約的","The conference room is booked all afternoon.","會議室整個下午都被預約了。"],["planner","/ˈplænər/","n.","行事曆本；規劃者","I write all my appointments in my planner.","我把所有約會都寫在行事曆本裡。"],["notification","/ˌnoʊtɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","通知","You will receive a notification when it's approved.","核准後您會收到通知。"],["informative","/ɪnˈfɔːrmətɪv/","adj.","資訊豐富的","The orientation was short but informative.","新人說明會雖短但內容充實。"],["brief","/briːf/","adj./v.","簡短的；向……簡報","Let me brief you on today's schedule.","讓我向你簡報今天的行程。"],["briefing","/ˈbriːfɪŋ/","n.","簡報、說明會","There is a safety briefing at eight.","八點有安全說明會。"],["clarify","/ˈklærəfaɪ/","v.","釐清、說明","Could you clarify the new leave policy?","可以說明一下新的請假政策嗎？"],["clarification","/ˌklærəfɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","澄清、說明","I need clarification on my job duties.","我需要釐清我的工作職責。"],["misunderstanding","/ˌmɪsʌndərˈstændɪŋ/","n.","誤會","Sorry for the misunderstanding about the date.","很抱歉日期的事造成誤會。"],["miscommunication","/ˌmɪskəˌmjuːnɪˈkeɪʃən/","n.","溝通不良","The error was caused by miscommunication.","這個錯誤是溝通不良造成的。"],["prompt reply","/ˌprɑːmpt rɪˈplaɪ/","phr.","迅速回覆","Thank you for your prompt reply.","感謝您迅速回覆。"],["courtesy","/ˈkɝːtəsi/","n.","禮貌","Please treat every caller with courtesy.","請禮貌對待每位來電者。"],["formal","/ˈfɔːrməl/","adj.","正式的","Use formal language in business emails.","商業郵件請使用正式用語。"],["informal","/ɪnˈfɔːrməl/","adj.","非正式的","We had an informal chat over coffee.","我們喝咖啡時非正式地聊了聊。"],["tone","/toʊn/","n.","語氣","Keep a friendly tone in customer emails.","客戶郵件要保持友善的語氣。"],["revision","/rɪˈvɪʒən/","n.","修訂","The handbook needs a few revisions.","員工手冊需要做些修訂。"],["edit","/ˈedɪt/","v.","編輯","Can you edit this letter before I send it?","我寄出前你能幫我編輯這封信嗎？"],["acquaintance","/əˈkweɪntəns/","n.","熟人；相識的人","I met a business acquaintance at the trade fair.","我在商展上遇到一位生意上的熟人。"],["activate","/ˈæktəˌveɪt/","v.","啟用；啟動","Please activate your new access card before Monday.","請在週一前啟用您的新門禁卡。"],["administer","/ədˈmɪnəstɚ/","v.","管理；執行；施行","The HR department will administer the employee survey.","人資部會負責執行員工問卷調查。"],["advisory","/ədˈvaɪzəri/","adj./n.","諮詢的；公告、警示","The firm has hired an advisory committee on overseas expansion.","公司聘請了一個海外擴張諮詢委員會。"],["annually","/ˈænjuəli/","adv.","每年；一年一次","Salaries are reviewed annually in December.","薪資每年十二月檢討一次。"],["attire","/əˈtaɪr/","n.","服裝；衣著","Business attire is required for the awards dinner.","頒獎晚宴須穿著商務正裝。"],["probation","/proʊˈbeɪʃən/","n.","試用期","New staff are on probation for the first three months.","新員工前三個月為試用期。"],["startup","/ˈstɑrtˌʌp/","n.","新創公司","The startup raised two million dollars from investors.","這家新創公司向投資人募得兩百萬美元。"],["qualifications","/ˌkwɑləfəˈkeɪʃənz/","n.","資格；學經歷條件","Applicants with the right qualifications will be contacted.","具備合適資格的應徵者將會接獲通知。"],["registrant","/ˈrɛdʒɪstrənt/","n.","登記者；報名者","Each registrant will receive a name badge at the door.","每位報名者會在門口領到名牌。"],["keynote","/ˈkiˌnoʊt/","n./adj.","主題演講；主旨的","The CEO will deliver the keynote at the conference.","執行長將在大會上發表主題演講。"],["networking","/ˈnɛtˌwɝkɪŋ/","n.","建立人脈；交流","The reception is a great chance for networking.","這場招待會是拓展人脈的好機會。"],["ranking","/ˈræŋkɪŋ/","n.","排名","Our hotel rose to third place in the customer ranking.","我們飯店在顧客評比排名中升到第三名。"],["adjustable","/əˈdʒʌstəbəl/","adj.","可調整的","All new office chairs have adjustable armrests.","所有新辦公椅都有可調式扶手。"],["affix","/əˈfɪks/","v.","貼上；附上","Please affix the label to the top of each box.","請把標籤貼在每個箱子的上方。"],["alternate","/ˈɔltɚˌneɪt/","v./adj.","輪流；交替的；替代的","Team members alternate weekend shifts every month.","團隊成員每月輪流值週末班。"],["anonymous","/əˈnɑnəməs/","adj.","匿名的","The employee survey is completely anonymous.","員工問卷完全是匿名的。"],["applaud","/əˈplɔd/","v.","鼓掌；稱讚","The audience applauded the speaker's presentation.","觀眾為講者的簡報鼓掌。"],["appreciative","/əˈpriʃətɪv/","adj.","感激的；讚賞的","We are appreciative of your continued business.","我們很感謝您持續的惠顧。"],["attentively","/əˈtɛntɪvli/","adv.","專注地；用心地","The trainees listened attentively to the safety briefing.","受訓人員專心聆聽安全簡報。"],["autograph","/ˈɔtəˌɡræf/","n./v.","親筆簽名；簽名","The author will autograph copies of her book after the talk.","作者將在演講後為她的書簽名。"],["belated","/bɪˈleɪtɪd/","adj.","遲來的；延誤的","Please accept our belated thanks for your generous donation.","請接受我們對您慷慨捐款遲來的感謝。"],["blend","/blɛnd/","v./n.","混合；融合","Our coffee is a blend of beans from three countries.","我們的咖啡是由三個國家的咖啡豆混合而成。"],["boast","/boʊst/","v.","以擁有…自豪；誇耀","The new hotel boasts an outdoor pool and a fitness center.","新飯店擁有戶外泳池和健身中心。"],["booming","/ˈbumɪŋ/","adj.","蓬勃發展的；興旺的","The company opened a branch in the booming tech district.","公司在蓬勃發展的科技園區開設了分公司。"],["broaden","/ˈbrɔdən/","v.","擴大；拓寬","We hope to broaden our customer base in Southeast Asia.","我們希望擴大在東南亞的客群。"],["bustling","/ˈbʌslɪŋ/","adj.","熙熙攘攘的；繁忙的","The store is located in a bustling shopping district.","這家店位於熱鬧的購物區。"],["cautiously","/ˈkɔʃəsli/","adv.","謹慎地","Investors are reacting cautiously to the merger news.","投資人對合併消息反應謹慎。"],["celebrated","/ˈsɛləˌbreɪtɪd/","adj.","著名的；有名的","A celebrated chef will cook at our opening dinner.","一位知名主廚將在我們的開幕晚宴掌廚。"],["chronological","/ˌkrɑnəˈlɑdʒɪkəl/","adj.","按時間順序的","List your work experience in reverse chronological order.","請按時間倒序列出您的工作經歷。"],["confidentially","/ˌkɑnfəˈdɛnʃəli/","adv.","機密地；私下地","All applications will be handled confidentially.","所有申請都將以機密方式處理。"],["conveniently","/kənˈvinjəntli/","adv.","便利地","The hotel is conveniently located near the train station.","飯店位於火車站附近，交通便利。"],["craftsmanship","/ˈkræftsmənˌʃɪp/","n.","工藝；手藝","Our furniture is known for its fine craftsmanship.","我們的家具以精湛工藝聞名。"],["customarily","/ˌkʌstəˈmɛrəli/","adv.","按慣例；通常","Bonuses are customarily paid at the end of the year.","獎金通常在年底發放。"],["delicate","/ˈdɛlɪkət/","adj.","易碎的；精緻的；微妙的","Please handle these delicate glass items with care.","請小心處理這些易碎的玻璃製品。"],["drastically","/ˈdræstɪkli/","adv.","大幅地；劇烈地","Shipping costs have increased drastically this year.","今年運費大幅上漲。"],["enlarge","/ɪnˈlɑrdʒ/","v.","放大；擴大","Could you enlarge this chart for the presentation slides?","你可以把這張圖表放大用在簡報上嗎？"],["enthusiastically","/ɪnˌθuziˈæstɪkli/","adv.","熱情地；熱烈地","The staff responded enthusiastically to the new bonus plan.","員工對新的獎金方案反應熱烈。"],["equip","/ɪˈkwɪp/","v.","配備；裝備","Every meeting room is equipped with a projector.","每間會議室都配有投影機。"],["equivalent","/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/","adj./n.","相等的；同等物","Applicants need a bachelor's degree or equivalent experience.","應徵者需具備學士學位或同等經驗。"],["extensively","/ɪkˈstɛnsɪvli/","adv.","廣泛地；大規模地","The product was tested extensively before its release.","這項產品上市前經過廣泛測試。"],["favorably","/ˈfeɪvərəbli/","adv.","有利地；贊同地","Customers have responded favorably to the new design.","顧客對新設計反應良好。"],["flawless","/ˈflɔləs/","adj.","完美無瑕的","Thanks to careful planning, the event was flawless.","多虧周詳的規劃，活動進行得完美無缺。"],["furnish","/ˈfɝnɪʃ/","v.","配備家具；提供","The apartments are fully furnished for business travelers.","這些公寓為商務旅客提供全套家具。"],["gratitude","/ˈɡrætəˌtud/","n.","感謝；感激","We would like to express our gratitude to all our sponsors.","我們要向所有贊助商表達感謝。"],["ideally","/aɪˈdiəli/","adv.","理想的情況是；最好","Ideally, the report should be finished by Thursday.","最好報告能在週四前完成。"],["illegible","/ɪˈlɛdʒəbəl/","adj.","難以辨認的；字跡潦草的","The signature on the form is illegible.","表格上的簽名難以辨認。"],["indefinitely","/ɪnˈdɛfənətli/","adv.","無限期地","The product launch has been postponed indefinitely.","產品發表會已無限期延後。"],["intuitive","/ɪnˈtuətɪv/","adj.","直覺的；容易上手的","The new booking system has an intuitive interface.","新的訂位系統介面直覺易用。"],["inviting","/ɪnˈvaɪtɪŋ/","adj.","吸引人的；誘人的","The renovated café has a warm and inviting atmosphere.","翻新後的咖啡廳氣氛溫馨又吸引人。"],["knowledgeable","/ˈnɑlɪdʒəbəl/","adj.","知識淵博的；內行的","Our sales staff are knowledgeable about every product.","我們的銷售人員對每項產品都很熟悉。"],["lag","/læɡ/","v./n.","落後；延遲","Sales in the northern region lag behind last year's figures.","北區的銷售落後去年的數字。"],["legibly","/ˈlɛdʒəbli/","adv.","字跡清楚地","Please print your name legibly on the registration form.","請在報名表上清楚寫下您的姓名。"],["modestly","/ˈmɑdɪstli/","adv.","適度地；謙虛地","Profits rose modestly in the third quarter.","第三季利潤小幅上升。"],["momentarily","/ˌmoʊmənˈtɛrəli/","adv.","片刻；馬上","The doctor will be with you momentarily.","醫生馬上就來為您看診。"],["noticeably","/ˈnoʊtɪsəbli/","adv.","明顯地","Customer complaints have decreased noticeably this month.","本月客訴明顯減少。"],["occupied","/ˈɑkjəˌpaɪd/","adj.","使用中的；忙碌的","All the meeting rooms are occupied this morning.","今天上午所有會議室都有人使用。"],["outgoing","/ˈaʊtˌɡoʊɪŋ/","adj.","外向的；即將離任的；外寄的","We thanked the outgoing president for her years of service.","我們感謝即將卸任的總裁多年來的貢獻。"],["preferably","/ˈprɛfərəbli/","adv.","最好是；更可取地","Please reply by Friday, preferably by email.","請於週五前回覆，最好用電子郵件。"],["reliably","/rɪˈlaɪəbli/","adv.","可靠地","The new machine has performed reliably for six months.","新機器六個月來運作穩定可靠。"],["remainder","/rɪˈmeɪndɚ/","n.","剩餘部分；餘額","The remainder of the payment is due upon delivery.","餘款須於交貨時付清。"],["repeatedly","/rɪˈpitɪdli/","adv.","一再地；反覆地","The customer repeatedly asked about the delivery date.","那位顧客一再詢問交貨日期。"],["utilize","/ˈjutəˌlaɪz/","v.","利用；使用","We should utilize the empty storage space more efficiently.","我們應更有效率地利用空著的倉儲空間。"],["appealing","/əˈpilɪŋ/","adj.","吸引人的","The new packaging is more appealing to young buyers.","新包裝對年輕買家更有吸引力。"],["approachable","/əˈproʊtʃəbəl/","adj.","平易近人的；容易接近的","Our new manager is friendly and approachable.","我們的新經理友善又平易近人。"],["assurance","/əˈʃʊrəns/","n.","保證；擔保","The supplier gave us assurance that the parts would arrive on time.","供應商向我們保證零件會準時送達。"],["attendant","/əˈtɛndənt/","n.","服務員；侍者","A parking attendant will direct you to an available space.","停車場服務員會引導您到空車位。"],["encouraging","/ɪnˈkɝɪdʒɪŋ/","adj.","令人鼓舞的","The first-quarter sales results are very encouraging.","第一季的銷售成績非常令人振奮。"],["furnishing","/ˈfɝnɪʃɪŋ/","n.","家具陳設（常用複數）","The office furnishings were chosen by an interior designer.","辦公室的家具陳設是由室內設計師挑選的。"],["glossy","/ˈɡlɑsi/","adj.","光滑的；亮面的","The brochure is printed on glossy paper.","這份手冊是用亮面紙印刷的。"],["hassle","/ˈhæsəl/","n.","麻煩；困擾","Online check-in saves you the hassle of waiting in line.","線上報到可省去排隊的麻煩。"],["lecturer","/ˈlɛktʃərɚ/","n.","講師；演講者","A guest lecturer will talk about digital marketing.","一位客座講師將談論數位行銷。"],["plaque","/plæk/","n.","獎牌；匾額","She received a plaque for ten years of service.","她因服務滿十年而獲頒一面獎牌。"],["jot down","/dʒɑt daʊn/","phr.","迅速記下","Let me jot down your phone number before I forget.","讓我在忘記之前先記下您的電話號碼。"],["at the last minute","/æt ðə læst ˈmɪnɪt/","phr.","在最後一刻","The client changed the meeting time at the last minute.","客戶在最後一刻更改了會議時間。"],["be out of the office","/bi aʊt əv ði ˈɔfɪs/","phr.","不在辦公室；外出","I will be out of the office until next Tuesday.","我下週二前都不在辦公室。"],["run a business","/rʌn ə ˈbɪznəs/","phr.","經營事業","She has run a business in Taipei for fifteen years.","她在台北經營事業已有十五年。"],["place an ad","/pleɪs ən æd/","phr.","刊登廣告","We plan to place an ad in the local newspaper.","我們打算在地方報紙刊登廣告。"],["post a notice","/poʊst ə ˈnoʊtɪs/","phr.","張貼公告","Please post a notice about the elevator repair in the lobby.","請在大廳張貼電梯維修的公告。"],["submit a proposal","/səbˈmɪt ə prəˈpoʊzəl/","phr.","提交提案","All teams must submit a proposal by the end of May.","所有團隊必須在五月底前提交提案。"],["file a complaint","/faɪl ə kəmˈpleɪnt/","phr.","提出申訴；投訴","The customer decided to file a complaint about the late delivery.","那位顧客決定針對延遲送貨提出申訴。"],["handle a complaint","/ˈhændəl ə kəmˈpleɪnt/","phr.","處理客訴","Every clerk is trained to handle a complaint politely.","每位店員都受過禮貌處理客訴的訓練。"],["put someone through","/pʊt ˈsʌmˌwʌn θru/","phr.","（電話）幫某人接通","Could you put me through to the accounting department?","可以幫我轉接會計部嗎？"],["work in shifts","/wɝk ɪn ʃɪfts/","phr.","輪班工作","Factory workers work in shifts to keep production running.","工廠員工輪班工作以維持生產運轉。"],["sales pitch","/ˈseɪlz pɪtʃ/","n.","推銷說詞","He practiced his sales pitch before meeting the buyer.","他在見買家之前先練習了推銷說詞。"],["contact information","/ˈkɑntækt ˌɪnfɚˈmeɪʃən/","n.","聯絡資訊","Please update your contact information in the system.","請在系統中更新您的聯絡資訊。"],["team building","/ˈtim ˌbɪldɪŋ/","n.","團隊建立；團隊凝聚活動","The company holds a team building retreat every spring.","公司每年春天都會舉辦團隊凝聚營。"],["company policy","/ˈkʌmpəni ˈpɑləsi/","n.","公司政策","Company policy does not allow smoking in the building.","公司政策禁止在大樓內吸菸。"],["instruction manual","/ɪnˈstrʌkʃən ˈmænjuəl/","n.","使用說明書","Read the instruction manual before using the printer.","使用印表機前請先閱讀說明書。"],["employee benefits","/ɪmˈplɔɪi ˈbɛnəfɪts/","n.","員工福利","Our employee benefits include free health checkups.","我們的員工福利包括免費健康檢查。"],["working conditions","/ˈwɝkɪŋ kənˈdɪʃənz/","n.","工作條件；工作環境","The union is asking for better working conditions.","工會要求改善工作條件。"],["confirmation number","/ˌkɑnfɚˈmeɪʃən ˈnʌmbɚ/","n.","確認編號","Please keep your confirmation number for future reference.","請保留您的確認編號以備日後查詢。"],["capital","/ˈkæpɪtəl/","n.","資本；資金","We need more capital to expand overseas.","我們需要更多資金拓展海外市場。"],["cash flow","/ˈkæʃ ˌfloʊ/","phr.","現金流量","Late payments are hurting our cash flow.","延遲付款正影響我們的現金流。"],["balance sheet","/ˈbæləns ˌʃiːt/","phr.","資產負債表","The balance sheet shows very little debt.","資產負債表顯示負債很少。"],["income statement","/ˈɪnkʌm ˌsteɪtmənt/","phr.","損益表","Revenue appears at the top of the income statement.","營收列在損益表的最上方。"],["financial statement","/faɪˌnænʃəl ˈsteɪtmənt/","phr.","財務報表","The financial statements must be audited each year.","財務報表每年都必須經過查核。"],["annual report","/ˌænjuəl rɪˈpɔːrt/","phr.","年報","The annual report will be mailed to shareholders.","年報將寄送給股東。"],["earnings report","/ˈɝːnɪŋz rɪˌpɔːrt/","phr.","財報；盈餘報告","Investors are waiting for the earnings report.","投資人正在等待財報公布。"],["quarterly earnings","/ˌkwɔːrtərli ˈɝːnɪŋz/","phr.","季度盈餘","Quarterly earnings beat analysts' forecasts.","季度盈餘超出分析師預測。"],["bottom line","/ˌbɑːtəm ˈlaɪn/","phr.","淨利；最終結果","The new policy improved our bottom line.","新政策提升了我們的淨利。"],["gross profit","/ˌɡroʊs ˈprɑːfɪt/","phr.","毛利","Gross profit rose thanks to lower material costs.","由於原料成本下降，毛利上升。"],["net profit","/ˌnet ˈprɑːfɪt/","phr.","淨利","Net profit was two million dollars after taxes.","稅後淨利為兩百萬美元。"],["net income","/ˌnet ˈɪnkʌm/","phr.","淨收入；稅後淨利","Net income grew by eight percent this year.","今年淨利成長百分之八。"],["profit margin","/ˈprɑːfɪt ˌmɑːrdʒɪn/","phr.","利潤率","Our profit margin on software is very high.","我們軟體的利潤率非常高。"],["markup","/ˈmɑːrkʌp/","n.","加價；利潤加成","The store applies a forty percent markup.","這家店加價百分之四十。"],["fixed costs","/ˌfɪkst ˈkɔːsts/","phr.","固定成本","Rent and insurance are fixed costs.","租金和保險屬於固定成本。"],["variable costs","/ˌveriəbəl ˈkɔːsts/","phr.","變動成本","Shipping is one of our largest variable costs.","運費是我們最大的變動成本之一。"],["operating costs","/ˈɑːpəreɪtɪŋ ˌkɔːsts/","phr.","營運成本","Solar panels lowered our operating costs.","太陽能板降低了我們的營運成本。"],["operating expenses","/ˈɑːpəreɪtɪŋ ɪkˌspensɪz/","phr.","營業費用","Operating expenses rose because of new hires.","因新聘員工，營業費用增加。"],["overhead costs","/ˈoʊvərhed ˌkɔːsts/","phr.","間接成本；營運雜支","Moving online cut our overhead costs.","轉型線上減少了我們的間接成本。"],["expense account","/ɪkˈspens əˌkaʊnt/","phr.","公費帳戶；交際費","Client dinners are charged to the expense account.","客戶晚餐費用記在公費帳戶上。"],["petty cash","/ˌpeti ˈkæʃ/","phr.","零用金","Small office purchases are paid from petty cash.","辦公室小額採購以零用金支付。"],["tax deduction","/ˈtæks dɪˌdʌkʃən/","phr.","減稅；扣除額","Business travel may qualify for a tax deduction.","商務差旅可能符合減稅資格。"],["tax-deductible","/ˌtæks dɪˈdʌktəbəl/","adj.","可抵稅的","Donations to the charity are tax-deductible.","捐款給這家慈善機構可以抵稅。"],["tax-exempt","/ˌtæks ɪɡˈzempt/","adj.","免稅的","Nonprofit groups are usually tax-exempt.","非營利團體通常享有免稅。"],["exemption","/ɪɡˈzempʃən/","n.","免除；免稅額","The company received a tax exemption for five years.","公司獲得五年的免稅優惠。"],["auditor","/ˈɔːdɪtər/","n.","稽核員；審計員","The auditors will arrive on Monday.","稽核人員將於週一抵達。"],["auditing","/ˈɔːdɪtɪŋ/","n.","審計；稽核","She has ten years of experience in auditing.","她有十年的審計經驗。"],["internal audit","/ɪnˌtɝːnəl ˈɔːdɪt/","phr.","內部稽核","An internal audit found several errors.","內部稽核發現了數個錯誤。"],["bookkeeping","/ˈbʊkˌkiːpɪŋ/","n.","記帳；簿記","We use software for basic bookkeeping.","我們使用軟體處理基本記帳工作。"],["bookkeeper","/ˈbʊkˌkiːpər/","n.","記帳員；簿記員","The bookkeeper records every sale.","記帳員記錄每一筆銷售。"],["fraud","/frɔːd/","n.","詐欺；舞弊","The bank detected fraud on my credit card.","銀行偵測到我的信用卡遭盜刷。"],["compliance","/kəmˈplaɪəns/","n.","遵守；法規遵循","All branches must be in compliance with the new rules.","所有分行都必須遵守新規定。"],["proceeds","/ˈproʊsiːdz/","n.","收益；所得款項","The proceeds from the sale will go to charity.","銷售所得將捐給慈善機構。"],["return on investment","/rɪˌtɝːn ɑːn ɪnˈvestmənt/","phr.","投資報酬率","The new machine offers a fast return on investment.","新機器的投資回收很快。"],["bond","/bɑːnd/","n.","債券","Government bonds are considered a safe investment.","政府公債被視為安全的投資。"],["stock exchange","/ˈstɑːk ɪksˌtʃeɪndʒ/","phr.","證券交易所","The company is listed on the stock exchange.","這家公司在證券交易所上市。"],["stockbroker","/ˈstɑːkˌbroʊkər/","n.","股票經紀人","My stockbroker advised me to wait.","我的股票經紀人建議我先觀望。"],["broker","/ˈbroʊkər/","n./v.","經紀人；仲介","Ask your broker about the fees.","請向您的經紀人詢問費用。"],["brokerage","/ˈbroʊkərɪdʒ/","n.","經紀業；經紀公司；佣金","He opened an account with an online brokerage.","他在一家網路券商開了帳戶。"],["stake","/steɪk/","n.","股份；利害關係","The firm bought a ten percent stake in the startup.","這家公司買下新創公司百分之十的股份。"],["go public","/ˌɡoʊ ˈpʌblɪk/","phr.","公開上市","The company plans to go public next year.","公司計劃明年公開上市。"],["listed company","/ˌlɪstɪd ˈkʌmpəni/","phr.","上市公司","Listed companies must publish quarterly reports.","上市公司必須公布季報。"],["publicly traded","/ˌpʌblɪkli ˈtreɪdɪd/","adj.","公開上市交易的","Publicly traded firms face strict reporting rules.","上市公司須遵守嚴格的申報規定。"],["privately held","/ˌpraɪvətli ˈheld/","adj.","私人持有的；未上市的","It is a privately held family business.","那是一家未上市的家族企業。"],["holdings","/ˈhoʊldɪŋz/","n.","持股；持有資產","The fund reduced its holdings in energy stocks.","該基金減持了能源類股。"],["holding company","/ˈhoʊldɪŋ ˌkʌmpəni/","phr.","控股公司","The hotels are owned by a holding company.","這些飯店由一家控股公司持有。"],["plunge","/plʌndʒ/","v./n.","暴跌；驟降","Oil prices plunged after the report.","報告發布後油價暴跌。"],["upturn","/ˈʌptɝːn/","n.","好轉；上升","Analysts expect an upturn in the second half.","分析師預期下半年景氣會好轉。"],["recovery","/rɪˈkʌvəri/","n.","復甦；恢復","The economy is showing signs of recovery.","經濟出現復甦的跡象。"],["boom","/buːm/","n./v.","繁榮；激增","The city is enjoying a construction boom.","這座城市正處於建築業榮景。"],["slump","/slʌmp/","n./v.","暴跌；不景氣","Sales slumped during the winter months.","冬季期間銷售額大幅下滑。"],["principal","/ˈprɪnsəpəl/","n.","本金","Each payment covers interest and part of the principal.","每期付款包含利息和部分本金。"],["in installments","/ɪn ɪnˈstɔːlmənts/","phr.","分期付款","You can pay for the laptop in installments.","這台筆電可以分期付款。"],["loan application","/ˈloʊn æplɪˌkeɪʃən/","phr.","貸款申請","Your loan application has been approved.","您的貸款申請已獲核准。"],["credit limit","/ˈkredɪt ˌlɪmɪt/","phr.","信用額度","I asked the bank to raise my credit limit.","我請銀行提高我的信用額度。"],["line of credit","/ˌlaɪn əv ˈkredɪt/","phr.","信用額度；授信額度","The bank gave us a line of credit for emergencies.","銀行給了我們一筆應急用的授信額度。"],["credit rating","/ˈkredɪt ˌreɪtɪŋ/","phr.","信用評等","A good credit rating lowers borrowing costs.","良好的信用評等能降低借貸成本。"],["credit score","/ˈkredɪt ˌskɔːr/","phr.","信用分數","Late payments can hurt your credit score.","延遲付款會損害你的信用分數。"],["go bankrupt","/ˌɡoʊ ˈbæŋkrʌpt/","phr.","破產","Several small shops went bankrupt last year.","去年有幾家小店倒閉了。"],["bankruptcy","/ˈbæŋkrʌptsi/","n.","破產","The airline filed for bankruptcy in May.","那家航空公司在五月申請破產。"],["outstanding balance","/aʊtˌstændɪŋ ˈbæləns/","phr.","未付餘額","Please pay the outstanding balance by Friday.","請在週五前付清未付餘額。"],["past due","/ˌpæst ˈduː/","adj.","逾期的","Your account is thirty days past due.","您的帳戶已逾期三十天。"],["settle an account","/ˌsetəl ən əˈkaʊnt/","phr.","結清帳款","We settled the account before the end of the month.","我們在月底前結清了帳款。"],["remit","/rɪˈmɪt/","v.","匯款；匯寄","Please remit payment within fifteen days.","請於十五天內匯款。"],["overdraft","/ˈoʊvərdræft/","n.","透支","The bank charged a fee for the overdraft.","銀行對透支收取了手續費。"],["overdrawn","/ˌoʊvərˈdrɔːn/","adj.","透支的","My account was overdrawn by fifty dollars.","我的帳戶透支了五十美元。"],["account holder","/əˈkaʊnt ˌhoʊldər/","phr.","帳戶持有人","Only the account holder can make changes.","只有帳戶持有人可以變更資料。"],["billing address","/ˈbɪlɪŋ əˌdres/","phr.","帳單地址","Your billing address must match your card.","您的帳單地址必須與信用卡資料相符。"],["billing cycle","/ˈbɪlɪŋ ˌsaɪkəl/","phr.","帳單週期","Charges appear in the next billing cycle.","費用會出現在下一期帳單中。"],["billing statement","/ˈbɪlɪŋ ˌsteɪtmənt/","phr.","帳單明細；對帳單","Review your billing statement for any errors.","請檢查您的帳單明細是否有誤。"],["itemized bill","/ˌaɪtəmaɪzd ˈbɪl/","phr.","明細帳單","Could I have an itemized bill, please?","可以給我一份明細帳單嗎？"],["payee","/peɪˈiː/","n.","收款人","Write the payee's name on the check.","在支票上寫上收款人姓名。"],["payer","/ˈpeɪər/","n.","付款人","The payer's details appear on the receipt.","收據上列有付款人的資料。"],["pay in advance","/ˌpeɪ ɪn ədˈvæns/","phr.","預先付款","New customers must pay in advance.","新客戶必須預先付款。"],["prepaid","/ˌpriːˈpeɪd/","adj.","預付的","Use the prepaid envelope to return the form.","請用預付郵資的信封寄回表格。"],["prepayment","/ˌpriːˈpeɪmənt/","n.","預付款","A prepayment of thirty percent is required.","須預付百分之三十的款項。"],["upfront","/ˌʌpˈfrʌnt/","adj./adv.","預先的；預先","The supplier wants half the payment upfront.","供應商要求預先支付一半款項。"],["cash on delivery","/ˌkæʃ ɑːn dɪˈlɪvəri/","phr.","貨到付款","We accept cash on delivery for local orders.","本地訂單可貨到付款。"],["payment terms","/ˈpeɪmənt ˌtɝːmz/","phr.","付款條件","Our payment terms are net thirty days.","我們的付款條件是三十天內付清。"],["on credit","/ɑːn ˈkredɪt/","phr.","賒帳","The shop sells to regular customers on credit.","這家店讓老顧客賒帳。"],["partial payment","/ˌpɑːrʃəl ˈpeɪmənt/","phr.","部分付款","We received a partial payment from the client.","我們收到客戶的部分付款。"],["reimbursed","/ˌriːɪmˈbɝːst/","adj.","已報銷的","Travel costs will be reimbursed within a week.","差旅費將在一週內核銷。"],["rebate","/ˈriːbeɪt/","n.","退款；折讓","Buyers can claim a fifty-dollar rebate.","買家可申請五十美元的退款。"],["financing","/ˈfaɪnænsɪŋ/","n.","融資；資金籌措","The project still needs outside financing.","這項計畫仍需要外部融資。"],["financial planner","/faɪˌnænʃəl ˈplænər/","phr.","理財規劃師","A financial planner helped me save for retirement.","理財規劃師協助我為退休儲蓄。"],["financial analyst","/faɪˌnænʃəl ˈænəlɪst/","phr.","財務分析師","The financial analyst reviewed the sales data.","財務分析師檢視了銷售數據。"],["chief financial officer","/ˌtʃiːf faɪˌnænʃəl ˈɔːfɪsər/","phr.","財務長","The chief financial officer presented the budget.","財務長報告了預算。"],["CFO","/ˌsiː ef ˈoʊ/","n.","財務長","The CFO will join the call at ten.","財務長十點會加入電話會議。"],["treasurer","/ˈtreʒərər/","n.","財務主管；會計","The club treasurer collects the membership fees.","社團的財務負責收取會費。"],["cost-effective","/ˌkɔːst ɪˈfektɪv/","adj.","具成本效益的","Video calls are a cost-effective way to meet.","視訊通話是具成本效益的開會方式。"],["cost reduction","/ˈkɔːst rɪˌdʌkʃən/","phr.","成本降低","Cost reduction is our top priority this year.","降低成本是我們今年的首要任務。"],["cut back on","/ˌkʌt ˈbæk ɑːn/","phr.","減少；削減","We need to cut back on overtime.","我們需要減少加班。"],["lower costs","/ˌloʊər ˈkɔːsts/","phr.","降低成本","Automation helped lower costs in the factory.","自動化幫助工廠降低成本。"],["shortfall","/ˈʃɔːrtfɔːl/","n.","短缺；不足額","We face a shortfall of $50,000 this year.","我們今年面臨五萬美元的短缺。"],["funding","/ˈfʌndɪŋ/","n.","資金；經費","The research team received government funding.","研究團隊獲得政府經費。"],["fundraising","/ˈfʌndˌreɪzɪŋ/","n.","募款","The fundraising event raised over $10,000.","這場募款活動募得超過一萬美元。"],["raise funds","/ˌreɪz ˈfʌndz/","phr.","籌措資金","The startup is trying to raise funds from investors.","這家新創公司正向投資人籌資。"],["donation","/doʊˈneɪʃən/","n.","捐款；捐贈","We made a donation to the local hospital.","我們捐款給當地醫院。"],["nonprofit","/ˌnɑːnˈprɑːfɪt/","adj./n.","非營利的；非營利組織","She works as an accountant for a nonprofit.","她在一家非營利組織擔任會計。"],["profitability","/ˌprɑːfɪtəˈbɪləti/","n.","獲利能力","The new strategy improved our profitability.","新策略提升了我們的獲利能力。"],["unprofitable","/ʌnˈprɑːfɪtəbəl/","adj.","無利可圖的","The company closed its unprofitable stores.","公司關閉了虧損的門市。"],["break even","/ˌbreɪk ˈiːvən/","phr.","損益兩平；不賺不賠","We expect to break even in the second year.","我們預計第二年達到損益兩平。"],["break-even point","/ˌbreɪk ˈiːvən ˌpɔɪnt/","phr.","損益兩平點","We reached the break-even point in March.","我們在三月達到了損益兩平點。"],["incur","/ɪnˈkɝː/","v.","招致；承擔（費用）","You may incur extra charges for late returns.","逾期歸還可能會產生額外費用。"],["incur costs","/ɪnˌkɝː ˈkɔːsts/","phr.","產生費用；承擔成本","We incurred costs for repairs this month.","我們這個月產生了維修費用。"],["thrifty","/ˈθrɪfti/","adj.","節儉的","Thrifty shoppers wait for seasonal sales.","節儉的消費者會等季節特賣。"],["economize","/ɪˈkɑːnəmaɪz/","v.","節約；節省","We economized by printing on both sides.","我們以雙面列印來節省開支。"],["monetary","/ˈmɑːnəteri/","adj.","貨幣的；金錢的","There is no monetary reward for the contest.","這場比賽沒有金錢獎勵。"],["fiscal","/ˈfɪskəl/","adj.","財政的；會計的","The fiscal report is due next week.","財政報告下週到期。"],["central bank","/ˌsentrəl ˈbæŋk/","phr.","中央銀行","The central bank kept interest rates unchanged.","中央銀行維持利率不變。"],["GDP","/ˌdʒiː diː ˈpiː/","n.","國內生產毛額","The country's GDP grew by two percent.","該國的國內生產毛額成長百分之二。"],["indicator","/ˈɪndɪkeɪtər/","n.","指標","Sales are a key indicator of consumer confidence.","銷售額是消費者信心的重要指標。"],["economic indicator","/ˌekəˌnɑːmɪk ˈɪndɪkeɪtər/","phr.","經濟指標","Housing starts are an important economic indicator.","新屋開工率是重要的經濟指標。"],["global economy","/ˌɡloʊbəl ɪˈkɑːnəmi/","phr.","全球經濟","The global economy is slowing down.","全球經濟正在放緩。"],["emerging market","/ɪˌmɝːdʒɪŋ ˈmɑːrkɪt/","phr.","新興市場","Many investors are looking at emerging markets.","許多投資人正關注新興市場。"],["currency exchange","/ˈkɝːənsi ɪksˌtʃeɪndʒ/","phr.","貨幣兌換；外匯兌換處","There is a currency exchange in the arrivals hall.","入境大廳有外幣兌換處。"],["denomination","/dɪˌnɑːmɪˈneɪʃən/","n.","（貨幣）面額","What denomination would you like the bills in?","您想要什麼面額的紙鈔？"],["counterfeit","/ˈkaʊntərfɪt/","adj./n.","偽造的；偽鈔","The cashier spotted a counterfeit bill.","收銀員發現了一張偽鈔。"],["retirement fund","/rɪˈtaɪərmənt ˌfʌnd/","phr.","退休基金","She adds a little to her retirement fund every month.","她每個月都存一點錢到退休基金。"],["insurance premium","/ɪnˈʃʊrəns ˌpriːmiəm/","phr.","保險費","Our insurance premium went up this year.","我們今年的保費調漲了。"],["time deposit","/ˈtaɪm dɪˌpɑːzɪt/","phr.","定期存款","Time deposits pay higher interest than savings accounts.","定期存款的利息比活存高。"],["mutual fund","/ˌmjuːtʃuəl ˈfʌnd/","phr.","共同基金","He invests in a low-cost mutual fund.","他投資一檔低成本的共同基金。"],["corporate tax","/ˌkɔːrpərət ˈtæks/","phr.","公司稅；營利事業所得稅","The government lowered the corporate tax rate.","政府調降了公司稅率。"],["property tax","/ˈprɑːpərti ˌtæks/","phr.","房屋稅；財產稅","Property taxes are due every November.","房屋稅每年十一月到期。"],["taxable","/ˈtæksəbəl/","adj.","應課稅的","Bonuses are taxable income.","獎金屬於應稅所得。"],["taxable income","/ˌtæksəbəl ˈɪnkʌm/","phr.","應稅所得","Deductions reduce your taxable income.","扣除額可以減少你的應稅所得。"],["tax break","/ˈtæks ˌbreɪk/","phr.","減稅優惠","Small firms get a tax break for hiring young workers.","小企業聘用年輕員工可獲減稅優惠。"],["tax credit","/ˈtæks ˌkredɪt/","phr.","稅額抵減","Companies can claim a tax credit for research.","公司可申報研發稅額抵減。"],["tax incentive","/ˈtæks ɪnˌsentɪv/","phr.","租稅獎勵","Tax incentives attracted foreign investment.","租稅獎勵吸引了外國投資。"],["tax filing","/ˈtæks ˌfaɪlɪŋ/","phr.","報稅；稅務申報","The tax filing deadline is May 31.","報稅截止日是五月三十一日。"],["accounting period","/əˈkaʊntɪŋ ˌpɪriəd/","phr.","會計期間","Each accounting period ends on the last day of the month.","每個會計期間都在月底最後一天結束。"],["keep the books","/ˌkiːp ðə ˈbʊks/","phr.","記帳；管帳","Her sister keeps the books for the store.","她姊姊負責替店裡記帳。"],["balance the books","/ˌbæləns ðə ˈbʊks/","phr.","收支平衡；結帳","We need to balance the books before the audit.","我們需要在查帳前把帳目結平。"],["financial records","/faɪˌnænʃəl ˈrekərdz/","phr.","財務紀錄","Keep all financial records for at least five years.","所有財務紀錄至少要保存五年。"],["proof of purchase","/ˌpruːf əv ˈpɝːtʃəs/","phr.","購買證明","Please bring proof of purchase for a refund.","退款請攜帶購買證明。"],["authorization","/ˌɔːθərəˈzeɪʃən/","n.","授權；核准","Expenses over $500 need written authorization.","超過五百美元的支出需書面核准。"],["sign off on","/ˌsaɪn ˈɔːf ɑːn/","phr.","簽核；批准","The director must sign off on the budget.","預算需要總監簽核。"],["cashier's check","/kæˈʃɪrz ˌtʃek/","phr.","銀行本票","The landlord asked for a cashier's check.","房東要求用銀行本票付款。"],["money order","/ˈmʌni ˌɔːrdər/","phr.","匯票","You can pay the fee by money order.","您可以用匯票支付這筆費用。"],["operating profit","/ˈɑːpəreɪtɪŋ ˌprɑːfɪt/","phr.","營業利益","Operating profit doubled from last year.","營業利益比去年翻倍。"],["sales revenue","/ˈseɪlz ˌrevənuː/","phr.","銷售收入","Sales revenue exceeded ten million dollars.","銷售收入超過一千萬美元。"],["revenue stream","/ˈrevənuː ˌstriːm/","phr.","收入來源","Online courses are a new revenue stream for us.","線上課程是我們新的收入來源。"],["source of income","/ˌsɔːrs əv ˈɪnkʌm/","phr.","收入來源","Advertising is our main source of income.","廣告是我們主要的收入來源。"],["liquid assets","/ˌlɪkwɪd ˈæsets/","phr.","流動資產","The firm has enough liquid assets to pay its debts.","公司有足夠的流動資產償還債務。"],["fixed assets","/ˌfɪkst ˈæsets/","phr.","固定資產","Buildings and machines are fixed assets.","建築物和機器屬於固定資產。"],["write off","/ˌraɪt ˈɔːf/","phr.","註銷；沖銷；列為損失","We had to write off the unpaid debt.","我們不得不將那筆未收帳款列為損失。"],["bad debt","/ˌbæd ˈdet/","phr.","呆帳","The company set aside money for bad debts.","公司提撥了一筆款項備抵呆帳。"],["reserves","/rɪˈzɝːvz/","n.","準備金；儲備","The bank has strong cash reserves.","這家銀行擁有雄厚的現金準備。"],["emergency fund","/ɪˈmɝːdʒənsi ˌfʌnd/","phr.","緊急預備金","Experts suggest keeping an emergency fund.","專家建議保留一筆緊急預備金。"],["purchasing power","/ˈpɝːtʃəsɪŋ ˌpaʊər/","phr.","購買力","Inflation reduces consumers' purchasing power.","通貨膨脹會降低消費者的購買力。"],["consumer spending","/kənˌsuːmər ˈspendɪŋ/","phr.","消費支出","Consumer spending rose during the holidays.","假期期間消費支出增加。"],["cutback","/ˈkʌtbæk/","n.","削減；縮減","Budget cutbacks delayed the project.","預算縮減延誤了這個專案。"],["overspend","/ˌoʊvərˈspend/","v.","超支","The marketing team overspent by twenty percent.","行銷團隊超支了百分之二十。"],["budget proposal","/ˈbʌdʒɪt prəˌpoʊzəl/","phr.","預算提案","Submit your budget proposal by next Friday.","請在下週五前提交預算提案。"],["draw up a budget","/ˌdrɔː ʌp ə ˈbʌdʒɪt/","phr.","擬定預算","Each manager must draw up a budget for next year.","每位經理都必須擬定明年的預算。"],["budget approval","/ˈbʌdʒɪt əˌpruːvəl/","phr.","預算核准","We are still waiting for budget approval.","我們還在等預算核准。"],["financial difficulty","/faɪˌnænʃəl ˈdɪfɪkəlti/","phr.","財務困難","The store closed due to financial difficulties.","這家店因財務困難而歇業。"],["financial crisis","/faɪˌnænʃəl ˈkraɪsɪs/","phr.","金融危機","Many banks failed during the financial crisis.","金融危機期間許多銀行倒閉。"],["exceed expectations","/ɪkˌsiːd ˌekspekˈteɪʃənz/","phr.","超出預期","Third-quarter sales exceeded expectations.","第三季銷售額超出預期。"],["fall short of","/ˌfɔːl ˈʃɔːrt əv/","phr.","未達到","Revenue fell short of our target.","營收未達到我們的目標。"],["repayment","/rɪˈpeɪmənt/","n.","償還；還款","Loan repayments begin next month.","貸款從下個月開始還款。"],["interest payment","/ˈɪntrəst ˌpeɪmənt/","phr.","利息支付","Our monthly interest payments are rising.","我們每月支付的利息正在增加。"],["lump sum","/ˌlʌmp ˈsʌm/","phr.","一次付清的款項；一筆總額","She received a lump sum when she retired.","她退休時領到一筆一次性款項。"],["gross pay","/ˌɡroʊs ˈpeɪ/","phr.","稅前薪資；總薪資","Your gross pay is the amount before deductions.","稅前薪資是扣除前的金額。"],["net pay","/ˌnet ˈpeɪ/","phr.","實發薪資；稅後薪資","Net pay is what you receive after taxes.","實發薪資是你扣稅後實際拿到的金額。"],["pricing","/ˈpraɪsɪŋ/","n.","定價","We are reviewing our pricing for next year.","我們正在檢討明年的定價。"],["price hike","/ˈpraɪs ˌhaɪk/","phr.","漲價","The price hike angered many customers.","漲價讓許多顧客不滿。"],["wholesale price","/ˈhoʊlseɪl ˌpraɪs/","phr.","批發價","Retailers buy goods at the wholesale price.","零售商以批發價購入商品。"],["list price","/ˈlɪst ˌpraɪs/","phr.","定價；牌價","We sell below the list price for large orders.","大量訂購我們以低於牌價出售。"],["market value","/ˌmɑːrkɪt ˈvæljuː/","phr.","市值；市場價值","The market value of the shares has doubled.","這些股票的市值翻倍了。"],["net worth","/ˌnet ˈwɝːθ/","phr.","淨資產；身價","His net worth is estimated at ten million dollars.","他的淨資產估計有一千萬美元。"],["investor relations","/ɪnˌvestər rɪˈleɪʃənz/","phr.","投資人關係","Contact investor relations for the annual report.","如需年報請洽投資人關係部。"],["breakdown","/ˈbreɪkdaʊn/","n.","明細；細目分類","Please send me a breakdown of the costs.","請寄給我費用明細。"],["cover the cost","/ˌkʌvər ðə ˈkɔːst/","phr.","支付費用","The grant will cover the cost of training.","這筆補助將支付訓練費用。"],["at no extra cost","/ət ˌnoʊ ˌekstrə ˈkɔːst/","phr.","不另收費","Installation is provided at no extra cost.","安裝服務不另收費。"],["hidden fees","/ˌhɪdən ˈfiːz/","phr.","隱藏費用","Our plan has no hidden fees.","我們的方案沒有隱藏費用。"],["renewal","/rɪˈnuːəl/","n.","續約；更新","The renewal fee is due next month.","續約費用下個月到期。"],["rebound","/rɪˈbaʊnd/","v./n.","反彈；回升","Stock prices rebounded in the afternoon.","股價在下午反彈。"],["slowdown","/ˈsloʊdaʊn/","n.","減緩；趨緩","The slowdown hit small businesses hardest.","經濟趨緩對小企業打擊最大。"],["stabilize","/ˈsteɪbəlaɪz/","v.","穩定","Prices have stabilized after months of increases.","物價在連續數月上漲後已趨於穩定。"],["strengthen","/ˈstreŋθən/","v.","強化；（貨幣）升值","The dollar strengthened against the yen.","美元兌日圓升值。"],["weaken","/ˈwiːkən/","v.","削弱；（貨幣）貶值","A weaker currency helps exporters.","貨幣貶值對出口商有利。"],["advertiser","/ˈædvərtaɪzər/","n.","廣告主、刊登廣告者","Advertisers pay more for space on the front page.","廣告主刊登在頭版要付更多費用。"],["agency","/ˈeɪdʒənsi/","n.","代理商、經紀公司","We hired an agency to handle our online ads.","我們聘請一家代理商處理線上廣告。"],["exposure","/ɪkˈspoʊʒər/","n.","曝光（度）","The trade fair gave our brand valuable exposure.","這次商展給了我們品牌寶貴的曝光機會。"],["impression","/ɪmˈpreʃn/","n.","印象；（廣告）曝光次數","Good packaging makes a strong first impression.","好的包裝能留下深刻的第一印象。"],["outlet","/ˈaʊtlet/","n.","暢貨中心、零售店；銷路","The company has three factory outlets in the north.","這家公司在北部有三間工廠直營店。"],["pamphlet","/ˈpæmflət/","n.","小冊子","Pamphlets about our services are at the front desk.","介紹我們服務的小冊子放在前台。"],["segment","/ˈseɡmənt/","n.","區隔、部分","This product targets the senior segment of the market.","這項產品鎖定市場中的銀髮族區隔。"],["wholesaler","/ˈhoʊlseɪlər/","n.","批發商","We buy our goods directly from a wholesaler.","我們直接向批發商進貨。"],["defect","/ˈdiːfekt/","n.","缺陷、瑕疵","Please report any defects within one week of delivery.","請於收貨一週內回報任何瑕疵。"],["boost","/buːst/","v./n.","提高、促進；提升","The campaign boosted sales by twenty percent.","這次活動讓銷售提高了百分之二十。"],["brand awareness","/ˈbrænd əˌwernəs/","phr.","品牌知名度","Sponsoring the event raised our brand awareness.","贊助這項活動提高了我們的品牌知名度。"],["brand loyalty","/ˈbrænd ˌlɔɪəlti/","phr.","品牌忠誠度","Good service builds brand loyalty over time.","好的服務能逐漸建立品牌忠誠度。"],["capture","/ˈkæptʃər/","v.","奪得、吸引（注意）；攫取","The ad captured the attention of young viewers.","這則廣告吸引了年輕觀眾的注意。"],["clearance","/ˈklɪrəns/","n.","清倉；許可","All clearance items are final sale.","所有清倉商品恕不退換。"],["clearance sale","/ˈklɪrəns seɪl/","phr.","清倉大拍賣","The clearance sale ends this Sunday.","清倉大拍賣於本週日結束。"],["comparison","/kəmˈpærɪsn/","n.","比較","The website offers a price comparison of similar products.","該網站提供類似產品的價格比較。"],["customize","/ˈkʌstəmaɪz/","v.","客製化、訂製","Customers can customize the color of their sneakers.","顧客可以自訂球鞋的顏色。"],["customer base","/ˈkʌstəmər beɪs/","phr.","客群、顧客群","We want to expand our customer base overseas.","我們想擴大海外客群。"],["customer satisfaction","/ˈkʌstəmər ˌsætɪsˈfækʃn/","phr.","顧客滿意度","Customer satisfaction has improved since we added live chat.","自從增加即時客服後，顧客滿意度提升了。"],["debut","/deɪˈbjuː/","n./v.","首次亮相；首次推出","The car will make its debut at the auto show.","這款車將在車展上首度亮相。"],["discontinue","/ˌdɪskənˈtɪnjuː/","v.","停產、停止供應","We have discontinued this model due to low demand.","由於需求低，我們已停產這個型號。"],["distinctive","/dɪˈstɪŋktɪv/","adj.","獨特的、有特色的","The bottle has a distinctive shape.","這個瓶子的形狀很有特色。"],["distinguish","/dɪˈstɪŋɡwɪʃ/","v.","區別、使有別於","Quality service distinguishes us from our competitors.","優質服務使我們有別於競爭對手。"],["emphasize","/ˈemfəsaɪz/","v.","強調","The ad emphasizes the phone's long battery life.","這則廣告強調手機的長效電池續航力。"],["exclusive","/ɪkˈskluːsɪv/","adj.","獨家的、專屬的","Members enjoy exclusive discounts every month.","會員每月享有專屬折扣。"],["expectation","/ˌekspekˈteɪʃn/","n.","期望、預期","The new product did not meet customer expectations.","新產品沒有達到顧客的期望。"],["expiration date","/ˌekspəˈreɪʃn deɪt/","phr.","有效期限、到期日","Check the expiration date on the coupon.","請確認優惠券上的有效期限。"],["focus group","/ˈfoʊkəs ɡruːp/","phr.","焦點團體（市場調查用）","A focus group tested the new snack flavors.","一個焦點團體試吃了新的零食口味。"],["giveaway","/ˈɡɪvəweɪ/","n.","贈品；免費贈送活動","We're holding a giveaway to celebrate our anniversary.","我們舉辦贈獎活動慶祝週年。"],["highlight","/ˈhaɪlaɪt/","v./n.","強調、突顯；最精彩部分","The brochure highlights the key features of the product.","手冊強調了產品的主要功能。"],["impulse buy","/ˈɪmpʌls baɪ/","phr.","衝動購物（的商品）","Candy near the register encourages impulse buys.","收銀台旁的糖果會促成衝動購買。"],["interactive","/ˌɪntərˈæktɪv/","adj.","互動的","The store uses interactive screens to show products.","這家店使用互動螢幕展示產品。"],["leaflet","/ˈliːflət/","n.","傳單、單張宣傳品","We put leaflets in every mailbox in the area.","我們在這一區的每個信箱都放了傳單。"],["manufacturer","/ˌmænjəˈfæktʃərər/","n.","製造商、廠商","The manufacturer offers a two-year warranty.","製造商提供兩年保固。"],["market research","/ˌmɑːrkɪt rɪˈsɜːrtʃ/","phr.","市場調查","Market research shows strong demand for healthy snacks.","市場調查顯示健康零食的需求很強。"],["market share","/ˌmɑːrkɪt ˈʃer/","phr.","市占率","The company's market share rose to 30 percent.","公司的市占率上升到百分之三十。"],["marketplace","/ˈmɑːrkɪtpleɪs/","n.","市場；（網路）交易平台","The online marketplace connects small sellers with buyers.","這個線上交易平台連結小賣家與買家。"],["maximize","/ˈmæksɪmaɪz/","v.","使最大化","We placed the display near the entrance to maximize sales.","我們把展示架放在入口附近以使銷售最大化。"],["merchant","/ˈmɜːrtʃənt/","n.","商人、商家","Local merchants joined together to promote the night market.","當地商家聯合推廣夜市。"],["on display","/ɑːn dɪˈspleɪ/","phr.","展示中、陳列中","The new collection is on display in the main hall.","新系列正在大廳展示。"],["overcharge","/ˌoʊvərˈtʃɑːrdʒ/","v.","超收費用、索價過高","I think the cashier overcharged me by ten dollars.","我想收銀員多收了我十元。"],["overpriced","/ˌoʊvərˈpraɪst/","adj.","定價過高的","Some customers felt the tickets were overpriced.","有些顧客覺得票價太貴了。"],["persuasive","/pərˈsweɪsɪv/","adj.","有說服力的","She gave a persuasive presentation to the buyers.","她向買家做了一場很有說服力的簡報。"],["pitch","/pɪtʃ/","n./v.","推銷（說詞）；推銷、提案","He made a strong pitch for the new software.","他為新軟體做了強力推銷。"],["potential customer","/pəˌtenʃl ˈkʌstəmər/","phr.","潛在顧客","We sent free samples to potential customers.","我們寄了免費樣品給潛在顧客。"],["premium","/ˈpriːmiəm/","adj./n.","高級的、優質的；保費；額外費用","Premium members get free delivery on all orders.","高級會員所有訂單都免運費。"],["publicize","/ˈpʌblɪsaɪz/","v.","宣傳、公開","We used social media to publicize the event.","我們用社群媒體宣傳這場活動。"],["purchaser","/ˈpɜːrtʃəsər/","n.","購買者","The first fifty purchasers will receive a free gift.","前五十位購買者可獲贈禮物。"],["questionnaire","/ˌkwestʃəˈner/","n.","問卷","Please fill out this short questionnaire.","請填寫這份簡短的問卷。"],["reduction","/rɪˈdʌkʃn/","n.","減少、降低","There is a big reduction on all winter boots.","所有冬靴都大幅降價。"],["release","/rɪˈliːs/","v./n.","發行、發布；新產品","The company will release its new tablet in May.","公司將於五月發表新平板。"],["sales figures","/ˈseɪlz ˌfɪɡjərz/","phr.","銷售數字","Sales figures for the third quarter look strong.","第三季的銷售數字看起來很亮眼。"],["sales representative","/ˈseɪlz reprɪˌzentətɪv/","phr.","業務代表","A sales representative will call you tomorrow.","業務代表明天會打電話給您。"],["sales target","/ˈseɪlz ˌtɑːrɡɪt/","phr.","銷售目標","Our team reached its sales target a month early.","我們團隊提前一個月達成銷售目標。"],["seasonal","/ˈsiːzənl/","adj.","季節性的","Seasonal products are sold only during the holidays.","季節性商品只在假期期間販售。"],["selling point","/ˈselɪŋ pɔɪnt/","phr.","賣點","Low price is the main selling point of this model.","低價是這個型號的主要賣點。"],["showcase","/ˈʃoʊkeɪs/","v./n.","展示；展示會、陳列櫃","The fair is a chance to showcase our new products.","這次展覽是展示我們新產品的機會。"],["showroom","/ˈʃoʊruːm/","n.","展示間","You can test the sofas in our showroom.","您可以在我們的展示間試坐沙發。"],["specialty","/ˈspeʃəlti/","n./adj.","專長、特產；專門的","The shop's specialty is handmade leather goods.","這家店的招牌是手工皮件。"],["spokesperson","/ˈspoʊkspɜːrsn/","n.","發言人、代言人","A spokesperson announced the product recall.","一位發言人宣布了產品召回。"],["sponsorship","/ˈspɑːnsərʃɪp/","n.","贊助","The company's sponsorship of the marathon was a success.","公司贊助馬拉松相當成功。"],["storefront","/ˈstɔːrfrʌnt/","n.","店面；店鋪門面","We redesigned the storefront to attract more people.","我們重新設計店面以吸引更多人。"],["subscriber","/səbˈskraɪbər/","n.","訂閱者、訂戶","The magazine has over 100,000 subscribers.","這本雜誌有超過十萬名訂戶。"],["target audience","/ˌtɑːrɡɪt ˈɔːdiəns/","phr.","目標受眾","The target audience for this ad is working parents.","這則廣告的目標受眾是上班族父母。"],["target market","/ˌtɑːrɡɪt ˈmɑːrkɪt/","phr.","目標市場","Young professionals are our main target market.","年輕上班族是我們的主要目標市場。"],["trade show","/ˈtreɪd ʃoʊ/","phr.","商展","We met several new clients at the trade show.","我們在商展上認識了幾位新客戶。"],["trial period","/ˈtraɪəl ˌpɪriəd/","phr.","試用期","The software has a thirty-day free trial period.","這款軟體有三十天免費試用期。"],["visibility","/ˌvɪzəˈbɪləti/","n.","能見度、曝光度","Online ads increase our visibility among young buyers.","網路廣告提高了我們在年輕買家中的曝光度。"],["visible","/ˈvɪzəbl/","adj.","看得見的、明顯的","Place the sign where it is clearly visible.","請把招牌放在明顯可見的地方。"],["viral","/ˈvaɪrəl/","adj.","（網路上）爆紅的、迅速傳播的","The funny ad went viral within a day.","這則有趣的廣告一天內就爆紅。"],["assortment","/əˈsɔːrtmənt/","n.","各式各樣的種類","The store carries a wide assortment of teas.","這家店有各式各樣的茶。"],["authentic","/ɔːˈθentɪk/","adj.","正宗的、真品的","All our bags are authentic and come with a certificate.","我們所有包包都是正品，附有證書。"],["back order","/ˈbæk ˌɔːrdər/","phr.","延期交貨訂單（缺貨待補）","The printer is on back order until next month.","這台印表機缺貨，要等到下個月才能出貨。"],["boutique","/buːˈtiːk/","n.","精品店","She opened a small boutique downtown.","她在市中心開了一家小精品店。"],["brand image","/ˈbrænd ˌɪmɪdʒ/","phr.","品牌形象","The scandal damaged the company's brand image.","這起醜聞損害了公司的品牌形象。"],["bundle","/ˈbʌndl/","n./v.","組合包；搭售","The laptop comes in a bundle with a free mouse.","這台筆電以組合包販售，附贈滑鼠。"],["buzz","/bʌz/","n.","話題、熱議","The teaser video created a lot of buzz online.","預告影片在網路上引起熱烈討論。"],["cater to","/ˈkeɪtər tuː/","phr.","迎合、滿足（需求）","The shop caters to customers with special diets.","這家店迎合有特殊飲食需求的顧客。"],["consumer goods","/kənˈsuːmər ɡʊdz/","phr.","消費品","Prices of consumer goods rose last year.","去年消費品價格上漲。"],["criticism","/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzm/","n.","批評","The company responded quickly to criticism of its ad.","公司對廣告受到的批評迅速做出回應。"],["digital marketing","/ˌdɪdʒɪtl ˈmɑːrkɪtɪŋ/","phr.","數位行銷","She has five years of experience in digital marketing.","她有五年的數位行銷經驗。"],["door-to-door","/ˌdɔːr tə ˈdɔːr/","adj.","挨家挨戶的；到府的","They hired staff for door-to-door sales.","他們聘請人員挨家挨戶推銷。"],["duty-free","/ˌduːti ˈfriː/","adj.","免稅的","You can buy duty-free cosmetics at the airport.","您可以在機場買免稅化妝品。"],["eye-catching","/ˈaɪ ˌkætʃɪŋ/","adj.","醒目的、吸睛的","The poster uses eye-catching colors.","這張海報使用醒目的色彩。"],["flaw","/flɔː/","n.","瑕疵、缺點","We found a small flaw in the fabric.","我們發現布料上有個小瑕疵。"],["high-end","/ˌhaɪ ˈend/","adj.","高檔的、高階的","The store specializes in high-end watches.","這家店專賣高檔手錶。"],["low-end","/ˌloʊ ˈend/","adj.","低階的、平價的","The low-end model lacks some features.","低階機型缺少一些功能。"],["hit the market","/ˌhɪt ðə ˈmɑːrkɪt/","phr.","上市","The new phone will hit the market next week.","新手機下週上市。"],["in bulk","/ɪn ˈbʌlk/","phr.","大量地","Buying in bulk lowers the unit price.","大量購買可降低單價。"],["issue a refund","/ˌɪʃuː ə ˈriːfʌnd/","phr.","退款","We will issue a refund once we receive the item.","收到商品後我們就會退款。"],["limited edition","/ˌlɪmɪtɪd ɪˈdɪʃn/","phr.","限量版","Only 500 pieces of the limited edition were made.","限量版只生產了五百件。"],["merchandiser","/ˈmɜːrtʃəndaɪzər/","n.","商品企劃、陳列人員","The merchandiser arranged the new items by color.","商品陳列人員把新品依顏色排列。"],["money-back guarantee","/ˌmʌni bæk ˌɡærənˈtiː/","phr.","保證退款","All our products come with a money-back guarantee.","我們所有產品都提供不滿意退款保證。"],["non-refundable","/ˌnɑːn rɪˈfʌndəbl/","adj.","不可退款的","The deposit is non-refundable.","訂金恕不退還。"],["packaging","/ˈpækɪdʒɪŋ/","n.","包裝","The new packaging uses recycled paper.","新包裝使用再生紙。"],["pay in installments","/ˌpeɪ ɪn ɪnˈstɔːlmənts/","phr.","分期付款","Customers can pay in installments over twelve months.","顧客可以分十二個月分期付款。"],["personalize","/ˈpɜːrsənəlaɪz/","v.","個人化、客製","We can personalize the mugs with your name.","我們可以在馬克杯上印上您的名字。"],["phase out","/ˌfeɪz ˈaʊt/","phr.","逐步淘汰","The company will phase out its older models.","公司將逐步淘汰舊型號。"],["placement","/ˈpleɪsmənt/","n.","擺放、配置","Product placement on the shelf affects sales.","商品在貨架上的擺放位置會影響銷售。"],["preorder","/ˌpriːˈɔːrdər/","v./n.","預購","You can preorder the game on our website.","您可以在我們網站上預購這款遊戲。"],["product line","/ˈprɑːdʌkt laɪn/","phr.","產品線","The company is expanding its product line.","公司正在擴充產品線。"],["public relations","/ˌpʌblɪk rɪˈleɪʃnz/","phr.","公共關係、公關","She works in the public relations department.","她在公關部門工作。"],["recognizable","/ˈrekəɡnaɪzəbl/","adj.","易辨識的、可認出的","The logo is recognizable around the world.","這個標誌在全世界都認得出來。"],["reputable","/ˈrepjətəbl/","adj.","信譽好的、有名望的","Buy only from reputable dealers.","只向信譽良好的經銷商購買。"],["sales slip","/ˈseɪlz slɪp/","phr.","收據、銷貨單","Keep your sales slip in case you need to return it.","請保留收據，以備退貨之需。"],["shopping spree","/ˈʃɑːpɪŋ spriː/","phr.","瘋狂購物","She went on a shopping spree after getting her bonus.","她拿到獎金後去瘋狂購物。"],["store credit","/ˈstɔːr ˌkredɪt/","phr.","購物抵用金、店內點數","Instead of cash, we can give you store credit.","我們可以給您購物抵用金，而不是現金。"],["supply and demand","/səˌplaɪ ənd dɪˈmænd/","phr.","供需","Prices change according to supply and demand.","價格依供需而變動。"],["take advantage of","/ˌteɪk ədˈvæntɪdʒ əv/","phr.","利用；趁機","Take advantage of our weekend discounts.","把握我們的週末折扣。"],["top-selling","/ˌtɑːp ˈselɪŋ/","adj.","最暢銷的","This is our top-selling perfume.","這是我們最暢銷的香水。"],["trade-in","/ˈtreɪd ɪn/","n.","以舊換新（的折抵）","Get a discount with the trade-in of your old phone.","舊手機折抵可享折扣。"],["unveil","/ʌnˈveɪl/","v.","揭幕、公開發表","The company unveiled its new logo yesterday.","公司昨天公布了新標誌。"],["user-friendly","/ˌjuːzər ˈfrendli/","adj.","容易使用的","The website is simple and user-friendly.","這個網站簡單又好用。"],["address a complaint","/əˌdres ə kəmˈpleɪnt/","phr.","處理客訴","The manager addressed the complaint immediately.","經理立即處理了這件客訴。"],["apparel","/əˈpærəl/","n.","服飾、衣服","The store sells sports apparel and shoes.","這家店販售運動服飾和鞋子。"],["attentive","/əˈtentɪv/","adj.","周到的、專注的","The staff were friendly and attentive.","員工友善又周到。"],["cardholder","/ˈkɑːrdhoʊldər/","n.","持卡人","Cardholders get 5% cash back on dining.","持卡人用餐可享 5% 現金回饋。"],["cold call","/ˈkoʊld kɔːl/","n./v.","陌生電話推銷","She made twenty cold calls this morning.","她今天早上打了二十通陌生推銷電話。"],["conduct a survey","/kənˌdʌkt ə ˈsɜːrveɪ/","phr.","進行調查","We will conduct a survey of our customers next month.","我們下個月將對顧客進行調查。"],["customer service representative","/ˈkʌstəmər ˌsɜːrvɪs reprɪˈzentətɪv/","phr.","客服代表","A customer service representative will be with you shortly.","客服代表馬上為您服務。"],["dealership","/ˈdiːlərʃɪp/","n.","經銷商、經銷權","You can test-drive the car at any dealership.","您可以在任何一家經銷商試駕這款車。"],["generic","/dʒəˈnerɪk/","adj.","無品牌的、通用的","Generic products are usually cheaper than brand names.","無品牌商品通常比名牌便宜。"],["in demand","/ɪn dɪˈmænd/","phr.","需求量大的、熱門的","Electric bikes are in demand this year.","今年電動自行車需求量很大。"],["in response to","/ɪn rɪˈspɑːns tuː/","phr.","回應、因應","In response to your complaint, we will refund the fee.","針對您的抱怨，我們將退還費用。"],["outdated","/ˌaʊtˈdeɪtɪd/","adj.","過時的","Our website design is outdated.","我們的網站設計過時了。"],["overstock","/ˈoʊvərstɑːk/","n./v.","庫存過多；進貨過多","We are selling overstock at half price.","我們以半價出清過剩庫存。"],["product launch","/ˈprɑːdʌkt lɔːntʃ/","phr.","產品發表","The product launch is scheduled for March.","產品發表預定在三月。"],["redeemable","/rɪˈdiːməbl/","adj.","可兌換的","The points are redeemable for gifts.","點數可兌換禮品。"],["resale","/ˈriːseɪl/","n.","轉售","These items are not for resale.","這些商品不得轉售。"],["respondent","/rɪˈspɑːndənt/","n.","（調查的）受訪者","Most respondents preferred the blue design.","大多數受訪者偏好藍色的設計。"],["shelf life","/ˈʃelf laɪf/","n.","保存期限、貨架壽命","This snack has a shelf life of six months.","這款零食的保存期限是六個月。"],["sneak peek","/ˌsniːk ˈpiːk/","phr.","搶先看","Members get a sneak peek at the new collection.","會員可以搶先看新系列。"],["stock up on","/ˌstɑːk ˈʌp ɑːn/","phr.","囤貨、大量採購","Shoppers stocked up on water before the storm.","購物者在暴風雨前囤積飲用水。"],["storewide","/ˈstɔːrwaɪd/","adj./adv.","全店的；全店","Enjoy 20% off storewide this weekend.","本週末全店八折。"],["swap","/swɑːp/","v./n.","交換","Can I swap this shirt for a smaller one?","我可以把這件襯衫換成小一號的嗎？"],["unsatisfactory","/ˌʌnsætɪsˈfæktəri/","adj.","不令人滿意的","The service was unsatisfactory, so I complained.","服務不令人滿意，所以我投訴了。"],["upmarket","/ˌʌpˈmɑːrkɪt/","adj.","高檔的、高消費族群的","The brand is moving upmarket with luxury lines.","這個品牌正以精品系列走向高檔市場。"],["walk-in","/ˈwɔːk ɪn/","adj./n.","未預約的（顧客）","Walk-in customers are welcome.","歡迎未預約顧客光臨。"],["wear and tear","/ˌwer ən ˈter/","phr.","（正常使用的）磨損","The warranty does not cover normal wear and tear.","保固不包含正常使用的磨損。"],["web traffic","/ˈweb ˌtræfɪk/","phr.","網站流量","The campaign doubled our web traffic.","這次活動讓網站流量增加一倍。"],["well-established","/ˌwel ɪˈstæblɪʃt/","adj.","根基穩固的、歷史悠久的","We are a well-established brand in Taiwan.","我們是台灣的老字號品牌。"],["price match","/ˈpraɪs mætʃ/","n./v.","價格比照（保證最低價）","We offer a price match if you find it cheaper elsewhere.","若您在別處找到更便宜的，我們提供比價保證。"],["advertising agency","/ˈædvərtaɪzɪŋ ˌeɪdʒənsi/","phr.","廣告公司","An advertising agency designed our new campaign.","一家廣告公司設計了我們的新活動。"],["product demonstration","/ˈprɑːdʌkt ˌdemənˈstreɪʃn/","phr.","產品示範","Join our free product demonstration on Saturday.","歡迎參加週六的免費產品示範。"],["satisfaction survey","/ˌsætɪsˈfækʃn ˌsɜːrveɪ/","phr.","滿意度調查","Please complete our satisfaction survey after your visit.","來訪後請填寫我們的滿意度調查。"],["complaint form","/kəmˈpleɪnt fɔːrm/","phr.","客訴表單、申訴表","Fill out the complaint form and we will contact you.","請填寫申訴表，我們會與您聯繫。"],["refund policy","/ˈriːfʌnd ˌpɑːləsi/","phr.","退款政策","Our refund policy is printed on the receipt.","我們的退款政策印在收據上。"],["partial refund","/ˌpɑːrʃl ˈriːfʌnd/","phr.","部分退款","We can offer a partial refund for the damaged item.","對於損壞的商品我們可提供部分退款。"],["in exchange for","/ɪn ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ fɔːr/","phr.","交換、作為…的回報","Get a free coffee in exchange for a short survey.","填寫簡短問卷即可換一杯免費咖啡。"],["defective product","/dɪˌfektɪv ˈprɑːdʌkt/","phr.","瑕疵品、不良品","Defective products can be returned within 30 days.","瑕疵品可於三十天內退回。"],["damaged goods","/ˌdæmɪdʒd ˈɡʊdz/","phr.","損壞的貨品","The courier is responsible for damaged goods.","貨運公司須對損壞的貨品負責。"],["under warranty","/ˌʌndər ˈwɔːrənti/","phr.","在保固期內","Your laptop is still under warranty.","您的筆電仍在保固期內。"],["out of warranty","/ˌaʊt əv ˈwɔːrənti/","phr.","超過保固期","Repairs for items out of warranty will be charged.","超過保固期的商品維修需收費。"],["extended warranty","/ɪkˌstendɪd ˈwɔːrənti/","phr.","延長保固","You can buy an extended warranty for three more years.","您可以加購三年延長保固。"],["apologetic","/əˌpɑːləˈdʒetɪk/","adj.","道歉的、歉疚的","The manager was very apologetic about the error.","經理對這個錯誤深表歉意。"],["retailing","/ˈriːteɪlɪŋ/","n.","零售業","She has worked in retailing for ten years.","她在零售業工作了十年。"],["outlet mall","/ˈaʊtlet mɔːl/","phr.","暢貨中心、Outlet 購物中心","The outlet mall offers brand-name goods at lower prices.","暢貨中心以較低價格販售名牌商品。"],["price-conscious","/ˈpraɪs ˌkɑːnʃəs/","adj.","在意價格的","Price-conscious shoppers compare prices online.","在意價格的購物者會上網比價。"],["value for money","/ˌvæljuː fər ˈmʌni/","phr.","物超所值、性價比","Customers say our lunch set is good value for money.","顧客說我們的午餐套餐很划算。"],["mark down","/ˌmɑːrk ˈdaʊn/","phr.","降價、打折","We will mark down all summer items next week.","下週我們將調降所有夏季商品的價格。"],["ring up","/ˌrɪŋ ˈʌp/","phr.","（在收銀機上）結帳、刷條碼","The cashier rang up my items quickly.","收銀員很快幫我結帳。"],["roll out","/ˌroʊl ˈaʊt/","phr.","推出、全面實施","The company will roll out the new app nationwide.","公司將在全國推出新應用程式。"],["launch date","/ˈlɔːntʃ deɪt/","phr.","上市日期、發表日","The launch date has been moved to June.","上市日期已延到六月。"],["release date","/rɪˈliːs deɪt/","phr.","發行日期","The release date of the new game is next Friday.","新遊戲的發行日期是下週五。"],["kick off","/ˌkɪk ˈɔːf/","phr.","開始、展開","We will kick off the campaign with a big event.","我們將以一場大型活動揭開這次宣傳的序幕。"]]});
